European inflation slid into food
Accelerated inflation, recorded in the euro area, is first due to the dizzying growth in the price of food products.
The increase in prices in November has been higher than expected in the 13 countries of the euro area, registering - after 2.6 percent in the month of October - an annual inflation of 3.1 percent - announced the Union Statistical Office based in Luxembourg.
Official forecasts were only likely 3 percent – Bloomberg announced.
The European Central Bank (ECB), unlikely U.S., British and Canadian issuing banks, did not cut the basic interest, on the pretext that the decline, along with rising commodity prices and the reduction in forced unemployment, would cause a spiral of inflation.
The ECB wants to keep the inflation rate below, but at least about two percent.
According to an analyst, the ECB is in trap 22: "you have to negotiate" about inflation so that later it does not have to intervene on this issue.
Inflation of 3.3 percent, registered in Germany, broke the twelve-year record; while in Spain it rose from 3.6 to 4.1 percent.
Inflation soared in the euro area as a result of galloping food and energy prices.
End-of-wheat quotes increased by 88 percent and soybean prices also peaked since 1973.
Likewise, much more had to be paid in 2007 for vegetable oil and dairy products.
The price of crude oil in the world market rose this year by 52 percent, reaching black gold almost US$100 a barrel last month.
According to the ECB, inflation in 2008 will jump from the current 2.1 percent to 2.5 percent, instead for 2009 it will decline to 1.9.
According to analysts, annual inflation will remain in the next 3 or 4 months around 3 percent, however the average annual rate will be 2.1 percent.
At the same time, the ECB is expected to reduce interest rates twice during 2008.
Gallup foresees a government crisis
After a long stagnation, by the beginning of December the support of the Young Democrats Alliance increased significantly, peaking since 2002, while the Gallup never before experienced such a low level - 13 percent - in the case of socialists.
The difference in the case of the safe voters of the parties - due to the greater steadfastness of opposition voters - would mean support of more than two-thirds (71 percent) compared to the support of one-fifth for socialists (20 percent).
According to the poll, the Democratic Forum and the Alliance of Free Democrats would not reach the limit necessary to have any parliamentary scale: their support within the totality of the population is two percent.
Among safe voters there are one percent more supporters on both sides.
The economic environment continued to deteriorate even compared to the previous lowest point - it has never been so high, 41 percent the proportion of those who judged the economic situation of the country especially badly, while another 46 percent believe that the situation is quite bad.
Families, after the most hopeful expectations of spring and summer, are now more pessimistic about changing their own economic situation.
With regard to the next year, the majority of the population has the deterioration of the situation and only one-tenth awaits an improvement.
In December, 71 percent of those consulted, higher than any previous Gallup poll, estimated that the President of Government performs poorly than well their functions.
13 percent of those consulted trust or rely heavily on Ferenc Gyurcsány, while Viktor Orbán has the support of 38 percent of those consulted.
54 percent of the population does not trust the Head of Government at all and 27 percent do not trust the president of the Alliance of Young Democrats.
One of the indicators of the configuration of the political situation is that, the proportion of society thinks that it is possible to control the discontent experienced against the person of the Head of Government without a change of government.
While after the riots of October last year 35 percent estimated that it would be desirable to keep the Government and the Head of Government in power, currently this proportion is only 20 percent, while the relative majority (33 percent) believe that the only solution is the holding of new elections.
Interest in the referendum is characterized by the fact that 60 percent of respondents to the question of participation responded that they would participate surely and another 20 percent said they are likely to participate.
By way of comparison, in "a general election to be held this Sunday" only 55 percent of the population would participate safely and another 15 percent believe their participation is likely. Based on the current intentions of the voters there is no doubt about the result of the popular consultation.
74 percent of the population would disapprove the payment of school entitlements, 79 percent of the service of medical consultations and 84 percent of hospital care.
If we look at these proportions only among the safe participants in the referendum, 81, 84 and 89 percent of voters would reject the introduction of study rights, payment for medical consultations and that of hospital care.
The most expensive is the Auchan, the Tesco has quintuplicated its prices
They maintained the average price level rise of 16 percent the hypermarkets of the Budaörs golden trade triangle, with the difference that this year VAT has not been increased.
Article by Napi Gazdaság
This year also increased by an average of 16 percent in Budaörs’s gold trading triangle the Napi newspaper’s usual Christmas basket, but in all the hypermarkets there was a growth much higher than a thousand HUF.
As in December last year prices had already "skyrocketed" in food supermarkets, this is how there was no drastic percentage increase compared to the high starting point.
However, it’s obviously terrifying for consumers the fact that what they were able to buy last year at a price well below nine thousand HUF, today they can’t do it for ten thousand.
Napi’s basket in the hypermarkets studied exceeded with a minimum of 91 HUF the psychological limit of ten thousand HUF.
And the highest-value basket was 10 573 HUF.
(in 2003 that basket cost 6800 HUF.)
The price of Unicum liqueur and fish remained almost at the level of the previous year, but there was a strong increase in turkey breast steak, walnut and poppy seed.
The price of wheat flour and bread followed data from the Central Bureau of Statistics, althus in the Auchan we have also found a kilo of bread for the price of 139 HUF.
Competition did not reduce the price of the product to less than 200 HUF.
It was also surprising in this store that the price of Coca-Cola with two-liter redeemable bottle cost less than 200 HUF, so that this product, even with the price of the bottle, cost only 257 HUF.
However, in Napi Auchan’s basket it was the most expensive, while Cora the cheapest.
According to our calculations, with respect to last year’s Christmas prices, Cora increased with 15, while Tesco and Auchan with about 18 percent the prices listed in the Napi basket.
Comparing last year’s most expensive basket values to that of the cheapest basket this year, the difference has been 12 percent, while growth between last year’s cheapest and this year’s cheapest has been 21 percent.
Mean growth was 1480 HUF.
Last year the average price growth was 1206 HUF, so that during last year’s Christmas in prices the increase in VAT was felt.
Precisely this process was the one that shattered commerce, supermarkets were visibly unable to make a decision on the price margin to be applied for each product and to calculate the effect of price change on consumption.
(If the trader poorly plans the speed of a product’s circulation, they may lose an important profit in the margin that fits the sales volume.)
The increase in the price of Napi’s basket reached such extremes as a result of the increase in VAT, that the most expensive was higher with 1720 HUF to the value registered in 2006, while in the cheapest the difference was only an 844 HUF.
This year there were no such extremes, since the highest price now has been 1630 HUF more than last year and the cheapest also increased with 1284 HUF.
Comparing the two Christmas seasons, there was a catastrophic growth in prices in less than 20 months, in the hypermarkets grew more than 30 percent the price of basic consumer necessities.
(However this does not necessarily confirm the figures of the Central Bureau of Statistics: this office, in the case of some basic necessities registered in the 12-month interval a price increase above 30 percent.
For example, in addition to wheat, also in the case of egg.)
According to Napi’s basket, in the latter case this seems almost impossible, because in the price of this product that was quite expensive already last year compared to the base, it was recorded, in the worst case just 10 percent price increase.
According to all indices, flour suppliers have a position stronger than those of egg, being able to impose the drastic increase in prices even on multinationals.
Hypermarkets don’t complain in the gold trading triangle, they constantly talk about positive outcomes.
According to our collected experiences, most of the consumers of the three stores visited are no longer interested in prices.
Of all products they buy large quantities, taking preserved foods by pallets.
On Wednesday morning, large queues formed in the three stores ahead of the boxes because the number of customers suddenly increased.
However, we have information that in the interior of the country sales volumes are lower, many multinationals complain to the survey institutes because the income falls below their plans and not only in the case of food, but also in that of household appliances.
In many hospitals you save with disinfectants
There have been several thousands of infections in the hospitals this year primarily caused by the improper application of antibiotics.
The prevailing hygiene circumstances in hospitals, the overcrowding of the beds and the overload of the personnel do not favor the control of infections - says the doctor-head of department of the National Epidemiology Center.
In many hospitals it saves even with disinfectants.
Not long ago it has been diagnosed a contagion with MRSA in the traumatology department of Hospital János.
In a man hospitalized after a serious accident the presence of antibiotic-resistant bacteria was detected.
The patient was isolated.
The same type of contagion occurred in this same hospital at the beginning of the year.
One injured from a serious car accident was discharged from the hospital and the same patient shortly after had to return to the hospital as a result of infection with MRSA and since then a significant surgical intervention has not been possible due to the presence of the bacteria in his body.
As of December 10 of this year there have been 1094 cases of hospital infection caused by multi-resistant agents in the Nosocomialis Surveillance National System - said Karolina Böröcz, medical-head of department of the National Center for Epidemiology.
This means that this number of infections caused by multi-resistant agents has certainly been recorded in hospitals, of the rest there is no information.
About two-thirds of infections (683 cases) are due to MRSA, i.e. methicillin-oxacillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus.
One-third of humans carry Staphylococcus aureus (SA) bacteria in their nose without causing any disease.
Infections caused by SA (e.g. inflammation of the throat, tonsillitis, skin infections, wound infections) react well to antibiotics and are easy to treat.
However, once it is exaggeratedly or unduly applied to antibiotics, bacteria that normally react well to antibiotics are transformed into bacteria that are very resistant to antibiotics and spread rapidly in inadequate hospital conditions.
They can cause serious hospital infections, for example wound infections or sepsis first to patients with transient or chronic immunodeficiency, patients with weakened organisms, the elderly or people with little weight.
In the opinion of the doctor-director of János Hospital there is nothing special in MRSA infection, these infections are daily in hospitals.
Infection should not be confused with the epidemic, MRSA is only absent - said Tibor Nyulasi - where its presence is not examined.
Resistant to antibiotics
"These patients are isolated, the nursing staff treats them in rubber gloves and mask and there are the right antibiotics for their treatment," said Tibor Nyulasi.
Hospitalized patients are previously screened to verify the presence of MRSA in their body, but infection cannot even be prevented in all cases.
It's not fashionable to take samples
It would be possible to prevent MRSA hospital infections in most cases, however the current national hospital circumstances do not favour the prevention of training and contagion with multi-resistant pathogens - says Karolina Böröcz.
As this infection occurs mainly in hospitals and nursing homes, hospitals should examine hospitalized patients and immediately isolate the sickers who carry MRSA in their bodies.
However, microbiological sampling is not fashionable in Hungarian hospitals.
This fact is also due to the fact that the National Health Fund does not fund these medical examinations.
So the majority of cases come to light when visible MRSA infections already occur in the patient — said the epidemiological center’s medical-department head.
The European Union makes stringent entrustments for the application of antibiotics in human medicine and there are also national directives to treat infections and pathological conditions.
It is necessary to insist that antibiotic therapy is targeted, i.e. microbiological examinations should be done to prevent resistance against medicines, but hospitals do not always meet this requirement.
Microbiological sampling is even less frequent in the case of traveling patients or in basic care - said Karolina Böröcz.
Saved with disinfectants
Scientific experiments have shown that in most cases MRSA is spread from one patient to another through healthcare personnel.
Therefore, hand washing, the use of rubber gloves and masks play a very important role, however also in this sense considerable faults are experienced in hospitals.
MRSA is spread through droplet transmission and direct contact between people, however in national hospital circumstances it is not always possible to isolate the infected patient.
What’s more, hospital wards are often crowded, beds are often very close together, albeit to prevent the epidemic, patients should be separated by at least 1.5 meters apart.
Unfortunately it can also be experienced - added Karolina Böröcz - that in hospitals of less favorable economic situation is saved with disinfectants, there are few nurses and many patients and that is why there is a greater probability for infection.
In the opinion of Karolina Böröcz, where adequate prevention measures are complied with, fewer infections of this type are recorded or the contagion of the pathogen can be stopped.
MRSA government programme
The treatment of transmission with MRSA is a huge expense for the National Health Insurance Fund, so in all countries it is fought.
In England, for example, there is a governmental programme to prevent and reduce cases of MRSA.
The program appears to be successful, according to data supplied, MRSA infections show a declining trend in England.
The European Centre for Disease Prevention and Control (ECDC) has among its priorities the prevention of multi-resistant agents (among these MRSA) and that of hospital infections due to these pathogens.
Negative the police commander’s breathalyzer’s control that caused a deadly accident
The official expert report has been made on the case of the deadly accident caused by district police commander XXII.
It can be excluded the possibility that he was driving drunk or in a stunned state since then resigned commander of the police of District XXII, who on Tuesday hit and caused the death of a passerby - reported on Friday Attila Morvai, a spokesman for the Attorney General's Office of the Capital, after having prepared the expert report on the case.
The expert report confirmed the result of the primary breathalyzer control that had already found that the former police commander did not consume alcoholic drinking before putting himself behind the wheel.
The then-district police police chief XXII, on Tuesday with his private vehicle dubbling Kossuth Lajos Street in district XXII hit a 55-year-old man, who intended to cross the street, but not in the pedestrian-designated area.
(This last fact, i.e
The passer-by lost their lives after being hospitalized.
For what happened, the police leader of the district resigned and requested his retirement, according to the police statement, because he was very moved by the case.
The investigation of the case is handled by the Budapest Investigative Prosecutor’s Office.
Attila Morvai also said that the former police commander from the beginning collaborated with prosecutors in charge with the investigation.
400 million euros more for infrastructures
Hungarian Finance Minister János Veres and European Investment Bank (EIB) Vice-President Marta Gajecka on Friday signed three credit-limit agreements in Budapest for a total value of 400 million euros to finance education, transport and environmental infrastructures, as well as the energy sector.
The European Investment Bank (EIB) approved in 2006 a budget of 300 million euros to finance transport and environmental protection projects, which will be carried out from the subsidy of the cohesion funds, of which the parties had previously signed a credit agreement worth 100 million, the contract they have just signed concerns the use of the remaining 200 million euros.
The credit agreement of 150 million euros is also intended to finance the budget of educational projects.
THE EIB approved a total of 300 million euros for this objective of Hungary, on the use of the remaining 150 million euros the decision will be made later, by extending the credit agreement.
The parties signed a contract for 50 million euros for innovations, which the budget will employ mainly for the innovations and research project of the University of Debrecen.
During the talks they also covered the issue of the construction of the 4th metro line.
It was agreed that by the time Hungary finalized with the EU the details of the financing of the Metro, they will return to address the issue that whether or not it is necessary to modify the original contract and how to do it.
According to János Veres, this can take place earlier in the first quarter of 2008.
Since 1990 the EIB financed a total of 113 projects in Hungary worth 8.4 billion euros.
The interest on the appropriations is adjusted to EURIBOR and the EIB offers a grace period of 8 years, with no commission to keep the credit available to the debtor.
Blaurge, the EU real estate paradise
The development of the Bulgarian real estate market is admirable - the attention of the whole of Europe is directed towards that previously unmentioned Balkan country.
What, where and those who buy on the EU's even cheaper market, that will quickly become more expensive?
Re/Max Bulgarian division analysis.
The preferred objective for real estate acquisitions in Eastern Europe is without a doubt Bulgaria, with its cheap apartments of the ski slopes and the villas of the beaches.
The mountain regions of Bansko, Borovec, Pamprovo and Vitosa are the most preferred, since on the Albena beaches, the "Côte Dorada", the "Costa del Sol", the old Sozopol and Nesebar, but more and more people are looking for properties also around Kavarna and Balchik.
According to Re/Max analysts in Bulgaria, sooner or later the central area of the country - such as Veliko Tarnovo, Gabrovo, Elena, Triavna - will arouse the interest of real estate developers and more and more people will buy properties in the especially cheap area of Rus.
In the same way the capital Sofia can be attractive, commercial and office spaces promise a rapid recovery of the investment.
Bulgaria is in the best way to become one of Europe’s most appealing golf paradises, and can thus be a prominent destination also during the other two seasons, in addition to summer and winter.
Therefore, cautious investors are already making their purchases, for example around Bansko.
In the opinion of the analysts, those who buy real estate in Bulgaria also strive to change their life and their way of life.
Most of the customers are English, but they also come from France, Belgium, Spain and increasingly from Romania.
Maltese and Cypriot promoters are also present and there are traditionally many Russian customers on the beaches of the Black Sea and in ski paradises.
Foreign clients can be classified into three groups - says Georgi Jankov, Re/Max's regional director in Bulgaria.
Those who intend to settle here buy new or renovated properties for a price between 50 and 100 thousand euros or old houses in poor condition between 5 and 15 thousand euros, to renovate them later.
They demand good communication and access, in addition to them the proximity of a large city, the shops and usually of a local doctor is important.
The second category is the buyers of chalets (Bulgaria in the month of December was included among the top 10 holiday destinations of the Germans).
Real estate investors who make their purchases in the hope of benefiting in the medium or long term are the third group.
The price of capital properties is constantly growing, since demand is increasing.
Although in the European Union Bulgaria has the lowestest real estate prices, in the last five years they suffered an annual increase of 21 percent
Rising real estate prices significantly outweigh wage growth.
Fodor and the six for hundreds of Hungarians
According to the Minister of Environment and Hydrology Gábor Fodor the meetings at the level of experts will end on Tuesday and Wednesday after the official inauguration will continue negotiations at the level of ministers on the post-2012 international climate regime.
Experts and politicians from 192 countries around the world deliberate on the Balí Roadmap on post-emission reduction efforts under the Kyoto Protocol up to 2012.
There are currently lively discussions about the individual between developing and industrialized countries.
The United States has already indicated that for the moment it does not want to negotiate on precise figures, although it tends to reach the agreement that compared to the situation in 1990, until 2020 the emission of gases responsible for the greenhouse effect decreases with 25 to 40 percent.
Another great theme of the conference is that if industrialized countries, in addition to reducing emissions, are or unwilling to offer material and technological assistance to countries in need.
An agreement was also reached on the aid to be offered to developing countries.
The support fund, foreseen in the Kyoto Protocol, will be led by a 16-member leadership council, probably within the UN Global Environment Fund (GEF) - writes the "Piac es Profit".
Six by hundreds of Hungary
On behalf of Hungary, the Minister of Environment and Hydrology Gábor Fodor supports the EU’s efforts to retain its cutting-edge role in global climate protection and to promote the signing of the new international agreement until 2009.
The minister stated that the EU is committed to reducing its gas emissions, responsible for the greenhouse effect by 20 per cent, compared to whether or not the “post-2012 agreement” will be signed and is willing to commit to reducing even 30 percent if the world’s other large developed regions and developing countries are also willing to make commitments according to their responsibility and capabilities.
Gábor Fodor pointed out that the signatory countries of the 1997 Kyoto Protocol committed to decreasing by 5.2 percent, among this the then 15 EU Member States committed to meeting an 8 percent decrease.
Hungary's commitment is to reduce by 6 percent the emission of gases responsible for the greenhouse effect with respect to the period between 1985 and 87, which our country will comply with - says the press release of the Ministry of the Environment.
There is much at stake in Bali, since within two years it will be necessary to sign the long-term international climate policy agreement, because if not, it is certain that its entry into force would be postponed for after 2012. In this case the reduction commitments assumed in the Kyoto Protocol would not be followed immediately by a new international emission reduction system, whose need was warned in its most recent report by the IPCC, an international scientific association
With this, the reduction of emissions would suffer a delay and could not prevent an increase of more than 2o C of the average temperature of the Earth, a fact that according to the scientists would have immeasurable and irreversible consequences.
The British Army Recruits on YouTube
British army units in a video distributor post recordings of actions filmed in Iraq and Afghanistan to popularize themselves.
First the British air force (RAD) took advantage of YouTube’s services: special units displaced in Afghanistan since March 2006 are uploading videos about their actions against the Taliban – the BBC reported.
These recordings made with mini-camers mounted on the helmets are controlled on Kandahar’s general body of operations, then sent to London to be uploaded to the Internet.
The political message is inevitable
There are already 139 recordings from the soldiers of the air force that have been loaded in this way to the Internet and their "channel" has already been seen by more than 75 thousand people.
The British Ministry of Defence was registered in the spring of 2007 under "defence headquarters" and publishes videos of actions perpetrated in Iraq and Afghanistan, while the Ministry of the Community of British Nations (Commonwealth Office) and the multinational forces in Iraq (MNFI) have their own YouTube channel.
Operation in Afghanistan
Originally the air force had uploaded the videos for recruitment purposes, but in the opinion of the Ministry of Defence they also serve to present to the public the true objective of the presence of the British army abroad.
This type of propaganda costs virtually nothing compared to conventional television recruitment spots – defence expert Gordon Mackenzie told the BBC – instead, they inevitably have some political message, since in a specific way they justify the raison d’être of military actions decided by the government.
The Americans prepared a video game
The army is also concerned about the fact that, in addition to highly edited and censored recordings, amateur videos also appear in the distributor, for example about the death of the soldiers: in the "official" propaganda films, a little hypocrites, officers speak at most losses, without however presenting the bloody part of the fighting.
In addition, the battlefields of Iraq and Afghanistan have already uploaded to the Internet numerous videos recorded in real operations, but the British army is only lately seizing this opportunity.
Americans use a slightly different way for recruiting with free-to-unloadable shooter video games called America’s Army, in which in the midst of a more or less real situation the player can put themselves directly instead of soldiers.
Tombola and salted cupcake at the ministries Christmas party
It does not seem very sentimental the working minister Monika Lamperth: instead of the Christmas party, she will hold a working meeting for her colleagues who will be able to dismiss the year 2007 with salted cupcake and coffee.
There is a ministry that will celebrate their party with live music, in another they will create the Christmas atmosphere in the hearts of public officials with tombola and a toast.
Party, Christmas atmosphere, concerts and buffet - that's how the power is amused.
Also the offices of the State are preparing for Christmas.
The biggest Christmas party will take place in the Ministry of Defense, but not for the workers of the Ministry.
On the Christmas of the Orphans will receive gifts the children of the fallen soldiers and for the Christmas of the Missionaries the relatives of the soldiers who currently carry out missions abroad will be invited. A reception for the press will also be offered.
This portfolio will allocate 25 million for the festive atmosphere of the end.
The National Development Agency (ANF) and the Ministry of Economy and Transport (MET) will hold a luxurious party with respect to the parties of the other wallets
The MET festival will take place in the House of the Future, with a total budget of HUF 4 320 000 and of the six hundred workers of the ministry the presence of approximately three hundred and fifties is expected.
In the party of the wallet will reign a Christmas atmosphere, artists will also perform and there will be tombola draw.
The Christmas of the ANF cost 4 700 000 HUF and was held on Wednesday in the building of the National Council of Administration of Justice (CNAJ) with musical concerts and dinner.
Renting the room cost one million HUFs, the rest of the budget was spent for the more than four hundred guests.
We have information that the workers of one of the ANF departments are also invited to another Christmas party that will hold a contest management company called the Hungarian Center for the Economic Development of community funds.
For this objective they rented the complete building of the Comedy Theatre.
The information has not been confirmed by CHDE SA, since we fail to communicate with the competent person.
You can attend without a suit
The CNAJ building not only hosted the ANF party, but also that of the Ministry of Justice and the Police, which instead of Christmas celebrated Lucia’s day dance on December 7.
The CNAJ of them did not charge anything for the use of their facilities.
Five hundred people participated in the dance.
The party began with the minister’s greeting words and after dinner there was live dance music.
Responding to [origo's] question they reported: to attend the dance it was not obligatory to wear costume or evening dress.
Health, work and local administration portfolios prepare for modest celebrations.
The Ministry of Public Health will organize a programme and a party for its workers in its own building with a budget of HUF 400 000.
Instead, Labour Minister Monika Lamperth does not wait for her colleagues for an official Christmas party, but for an end-of-year working meeting.
It has the participation of one hundred and eighty guests who - as reported by the press department - will have only coffee and salted cupcake, so the party will not cost more than 350 000 HUF.
The minister for local governments, Gordon Bajnai, on the other hand, will simply provide with his colleagues in the classroom of the Ministry for Local Governments and Territorial Development.
The Ministry of Finance (MF) will hold a Christmas party in its own auditorium with the participation of 436 workers.
The Christmas party will have a budget of HUF 2500 per guest - from this budget the reception with buffet and a toast will be paid.
Since János Veres is the minister, the workers of the MF all the years celebrate Christmas in the same way.
On the other hand, there will be no festive atmosphere, the official character will be given not only by the ministerial speech, but also by the afternoon schedule of its celebration.
The agricultural portfolio will offer a New Year’s Reception on January 20, Christmas will not be held in the Ministry.
The reception will be held at Vajdahunyad Castle in the Municipal Park and according to the portfolio, there will be a budget of 1000 HUF per person for the one hundred guests.
This - according to the press department - is going to be a very simple reception standing, which will be invited only to specialized diplomats, accredited in Hungary.
These receptions that are celebrated every year, begin with a brief greeting speech of the minister and conclude with a modest meal.
The Ministries of Foreign Affairs and Education and Culture will not hold any Christmas holidays - this is what the corresponding press departments told [origo].
In the press department of the environmental portfolio they were unable to report on the budget of the Ministry’s Christmas celebrations.
What is known is that more than four hundred people were invited to be held at the Museum of Applied Arts.
The forces of the giant strike are gathering
The League Unions and the National Federation of Workers’ Commissions will constitute on Friday a strike commission to coordinate Monday’s indefinite strike.
On Saturday there will be a protest rally, while on Monday - the day on which the final vote on the public health law will be held - will begin the labor strike.
This action will surely cause great difficulties in transport, since it will completely stop rail traffic and until 13 hours the workers of the Collective Transport Company of Budapest will also be on strike.
On Friday afternoon the League Unions will report on the details of their strike on Monday that will be held jointly with the National Federation of Workers’ Commissions.
It will also constitute the strike commission of the LEAGUE and the National Union of Machinists that will coordinate the actions on Monday.
On Saturday there will be a rally of protest, while on Monday the participating unions will pronounce on strike indefinitely, if an agreement is not reached with the government.
This means that - on the day of the parliamentary vote on the public health law - they did not report on the date of the end of the strike initiated.
If the National Assembly disapproves of the public health law, unions will immediately withdraw their call for strike.
On the other hand, if the law is passed, the strike commissions will meet and decide on the future.
Based on Monday’s agenda of the National Assembly it is also possible that only the public health law will be voted on in the very early hours of the night, or perhaps around midnight.
As a result of the strike that will begin on Monday, there will be significant difficulties in transport: the railways will stop working indefinitely, in the morning it may stop a part of the collective transport of Budapest and more than half of the intercity transport of buses of the Volán companies.
Simultaneously, in many parts of the country there will be the closure of half of the roads.
Numerous unions and civil organizations have joined the strike, their names are constantly updated on the League’s website.
Some unions announced their strike indefinitely, others in definite times.
Until Thursday afternoon the State Railway and the Free Railway Workers Union (SLTF) could not reach an agreement even on the minimum services, although, as the Christmas festivities are approaching, more and more people are traveling on the trains.
According to information received until now, from the beginning of the day until 13 hours will be on strike the workers of the Collective Transport Company of Budapest, the Airports of Budapest from 7 to 9 in the morning, will hold a four-hour strike the LIGA Unions of the Electrical and Thermal Energy Industry, the Unions of the Educators called for a strike of 2 and the Democratic Union of the Educators from 2 to 8.
The Hungarian Association of Physicians will speak on a national strike at alternative schedules and the Health and Social Workers’ Democratic Union (SDTSSS) that are part of the Trade Union Cooperation Forum, will hold a two-hour warning strike.
The most important of the four demands made by the League is that the government withdraw its proposal for public health reform and submit a new conception to a social debate.
The second demand is to gradually introduce the new form of pension calculation that will come into effect next year.
The third is that they ensure, even before 2010, in the case of advance pensions the possibility that the occupations that deserve it can enter the system.
The fourth reason for the strike is that the Railway Workers Free Union (SLTF) that is part of the League Unions, does not accept the proposal of the Ministry of Economy and Transport on the railway sidelines and await a different proposal.
Political Capital[b1]: In the country is increased the risk by the Hungarian Guard
According to the Risk Analysing Division of the Political Capital the activity of the Hungarian Guard, constituted in the month of August with the support of the Movement for a Better Hungary, from several points of view has increased the political risk of Hungary and the region.
In the "risk warning" of the company is written: in relation to the activity of the Hungarian Guard the greatest political risk constitutes the fact that "with the aggravation of the ethnic tensions existing between the Gypsy and non-Gypsy people of Hungary, even in the short term there may be violent ethnic confrontations."
The main reason for this is that the political strategy of the Hungarian Guard is probably the provocation of an event of this nature - added the representative of the research institute.
They affirmed that all this is due to one of the main faults of the protagonists of Hungarian political life: "the protagonists of public lives ceded the public debate of the Gypsy problem to the representatives of the radical and extremist political groups, who were able to base their political strategy on the discrepancies between Gypsies and Hungarians."
This aggravates the problem, impossibles normal dialogue, strengthens extremists and increases the likelihood of the outburst of violent conflicts - they estimate.
In addition to that, according to the research institute, the activity of the National Guard, as a result of the great attention of the national and international average, "significantly deteriorated the image of Hungary abroad, especially with regard to the stability and democratic development of the country."
They remind us that: from the autumn of 2006 it received increasing publicity and encouragement the reorganization of the radical and far-right groups of Hungary and that since the summer of 2007 numerous organizations that define themselves as "associations of national self-defense" have been constituted in the country.
"The common feature of these groupings is that they define themselves as civil organizations, while they openly proclaim the training of their members for defense - even armed - (civil defense, national defense, defense of public order), alluding to the ineptitudes of the police, of the army, i.e. of the State" - they add.
They affirmed: all this occurs in accordance with the method that tries to give a civil presentation to different political aspirations, based on the discontent of society with politics and political parties.
Well, highlighting the civil and the form of association in the case of these associations not only serves to avoid the legal problems of legal registration, but it is at the same time also a political strategy.
According to the analysis, the activity of the Hungarian Guard is a risk factor also from the point of view of neighborhood relations.
"In recent months, in numerous neighbouring states they referred to the Hungarian Guard as a potential danger, while the ultra-nationalist political figures of certain neighbouring countries want to justify their own anti-Hungarian policy with the creation of the Hungarian Guard.
All this influences the political stability of the region" - they added.
According to the research institute, the constitution of the Hungarian Guard is not an isolated phenomenon in Central and Eastern Europe, so political risks were increased throughout the region.
They wrote that the Hungarian Guard operates in a similar way that, for example, the Bulgarian National Guard, whose constitution was announced in August 2007 by the far-right Bulgarian National Union (UNB).
The constitution of the Bulgarian guard is due to the massive riots of the Gypsies that occurred in one of the neighborhoods of Sofia (Krasna Poliana).
Taking advantage of this situation, UNB decided to constitute the guard, arguing that the objective of the organization is “national self-defense”.
In his opinion, in the last 17 years there was "Gypsy terror" in Bulgaria, however the State remained impotent and indifferent in the face of the facts - recalls Political Capital.
They added: this initiative has sparked a lively discussion in Bulgarian public opinion.
As it was noted, it indicates the increased risk of ethnic clashes that certain Gypsy organizations in Bulgaria have announced that in order to resist, they will constitute their own guard.
As the functioning of the Hungarian Guard so far has shown resemblance to that of the Bulgarian National Guard, it cannot be excluded that Hungary’s Gypsies also react to the threat similarly, organizing their own self-defense – it can be read in the warning about the risks of Political Capital.
The director of investigations of Political Capital, Attila Juhász to the question of the news agency said: risk analysis is one of the activities of the research institute.
As he said, each year they publish their risk analysis and when they experience something that can influence the change in risk, they inform the public opinion, as happened in this case, publishing their warning about risks.
The party is not always spelled with red numbers
In Hungary, the law precisely defines the days that are spelled with red numbers on the calendar and it has already become a widespread practice that around the feast days - that the coming year will be less - the working days are reorganized.
Even in the EU or in North America the holidays are unitary.
Hungarian laws make a difference between a national holiday, a state holiday and festive days.
Festive days are fundamentally related to religious festivals and historical ephemerities.
We celebrate the New Anus as well: both the last day of the old year, and the first day of the new year is festive - the latter above all so that they can rest those who spent celebrating the old year.
Throughout the year we have eleven holidays written with red numbers on the calendar.
It is a national holiday on March 15 in memory of the revolution of 1848 and October 23, commemorative day of the 1956 revolution.
On August 20 we celebrated the foundation of the State, on May 1st the party of work, on November 1st and 2th we remember our deceased family and friends.
In addition, in our country are two-day feasts Easter, Pentecost and Christmas.
According to the calendar, our state, national or religious holidays rarely coincide with a weekend, which is why it often bridges when before or after the party there is a single working day.
In exchange for the extended weekends like this, during previous Saturdays you cannot be absent from work or from school.
He is the labour minister who regulates in his specific decree when you have to work exactly in exchange for the day directly preceding or after the feast.
This legal standard is mandatory for all employers and their employees, as well as for employees and public officials.
It is not mandatory instead for companies and service institutions that, due to their function, work uninterruptedly even during festive days.
This year the order of work can be altered only around the feasts of the end of the year: from December 24 it practically stops life in the country, since according to the experiences, most of the people "bridge" during the days between Christmas and the end of the year or take their holidays during these days.
The next year several of our parties will coincide with midia or weekends, so there will be less changes in working hours than this year.
First, the agenda will be changed around the party of work so that then, for four successive days, the workers can rest.
On Saturday, April 26 it will be a working day, so that in return on Friday, May 2, it will be festive day.
The other change is related to the feast of October 23: on Saturday, October 18, it will be necessary to work instead of Friday 24.
On the other hand, next year during the end-of-year party can rest, since from December 24 it will not work almost anywhere, even if the last day of the year is a Wednesday.
Six deterrent children to sour the lives of your colleagues
Emails that we forget to send, sound messages that we never receive, innocent lies that happen to us without realizing it: all of them are part of our daily Folklore" at work.
You have to decide if you adapt to small discomfort or consciously avoid confusing situations that can irritate others.
Advice.
Excuse me, I forgot to let you know you've been wanted from the marketing department," says one of your colleagues."
That's why didn't you go on a date?
At best you feel it and try to repair the matter, maybe call the marketing department to tell them that you forgot to deliver the message (this is the least usual solution).
In most cases the matter is resolved by apologizing.
Before proceeding to embarrassing explanations, it’s worth meditating on the things with which you can bitter the lives of your colleagues and consciously strive to avoid them.
Do you borrow something that's not yours?
There’s nothing more irritating than when you want to pick up a document, an office tool or your phone and you don’t find them.
Do you remind that yesterday you placed the stapler on the table, but for this morning it disappeared?
Do you find your lost pen on the table of one of your colleagues?
Don’t take anything away from your colleagues without asking for them, because they will rightly be angry with you for subtracting their stuff.
Don’t take envelopes or post-it from the office because it may be unpleasant when you need them immediately and they sell out ahead of time.
Gossip about the private lives of your colleagues?
There’s no good solution to stopping rumours that are already running.
Who, what are you doing and with whom?
Where and why?
Don’t pass everyone the information (conjectures) you have about the particular lives of your colleagues!
Don’t abuse your colleague’s trust when he shares with you his most intimate secrets!
Bury in yourself what you have heard and don’t gossip about your colleague in his absence, even though others also know things about him.
Are you on sick leave unjustifiably?
When you call the office and say that you are sick and your head unbearably hurts, you feel bad or well, you feel that that day you prefer to rest; think that others must do your work, your impostergable tasks, your work per term.
Don't annoy your colleague!
If you already know in advance that the next day you will not go to the office or something can happen to you, so you must stay at home, communicate them, so that your colleagues or your boss do not have to confront your absence the next day.
Hugs, chuckles, phone calls
Are you involved in your work, but are you abruptly removed from it the chairs of your colleagues?
Did you unintentionally hear a phone conversation that it would have been better not to listen?
Don’t disturb your colleagues with your humming, songs, conversations aloud (less when you make them above your head), patales, constant blasphemies, expressing your discontents aloud.
All these can be annoying, even if they aren’t delving into a project (writing, planning, organization) right now.
Are you blaming others for a mistake?
Don't blame others if you haven't finished something on time, you've forgotten to send an important letter or message!
Don't allude to chaos eventually reigning in the office, or the noise your colleagues make!
You must recognize if you have made a mistake that harms others and you must repair the fault!
Ask how you can repair your fault!
Do you feel too much at home at the office?
Jogging and sneakers: very comfortable habit for the house, but it is not suitable for the office!
Don’t see a comfortable jogging even if your occupancy allows!
Don’t be disarranged, respect your colleagues and yourself wearing everyday, elegant and beautiful clothes when your occupation so demands!
You lose interest if you want to meet public expectations
The car advances slowly in the usual morning traffic jam.
It sounds a strange compass on the radio: violin with electronic effects.
I'm turning up the volume.
It changes the rhythm of the music and to the previous tones the bass is added and then the voice of a female choir as a true jewel intervenes.
Channel mr2 plays Zagar's Wings of Love.
National musical life didn’t spoil us much with quality electronic pop.
But now it seems totally different this jam when you’re listening to Zagar’s new album.
Yonderboi appears. Some new and interesting songs of underground [b2]digital [b3]nacional are gradually changing the image and even it is again fashionable garage-style rock, breaks guitars, the national electro pop has shown: there are novelties under the Sun.
Balázs Zságer began his career in the city of Pécs, played in the whole of Yonderboi until he began his independent career perhaps because both can not be protagonists of the same ensemble.
With his project (Zagar) and his music, a mixture of jazz, danceable electronic music and pop, he tried to succeed, when he was asked for soundtracks [b4] cinematográficos (pl.
Ferenc Török Szezon).
The wider audience knew the ensemble that initially performed only in small clubs when wan2 magazine selected its first album released in 2002 among the fifty most important national albums, classifying Zagar, along with Yonderboi as almost the only national trainer of trends, capable of selling also in Western markets.
There is no doubt that Zagar and its ensemble are fashionable, but no one has asked them whether or not they wear this label.
The set reacted as it should react: it prepared a new and even better album.
The recently released album, titled Cannot Walk Fly Instead will be able to open new paths for them, although the title itself aims to establish continuity with the initial years in the city of Pécs.
For this title was one of the lines of the antique ensemble of Balázs Zságer.
It’s good the reference about the airy, about the flight, but in addition to the airy of the music, it now appeared – according to the spirit and trend of the time – the guitar that sounds louder, the effect of rock and roll.
With these songs he presented the album at the Millenáris György Ligeti, the singer who currently works in England with the ensemble The Puzzle.
The album includes a true success of the channel mr2 Petõfi which lately broadcasts from morning to night popular music. This station led to the ears of the high-flying music of Wings of Love, recorded with six Hungarian singers (Divas Underground").
Well, it's all in order (?).
hvg.hu asked Balázs Záger.
hvg.hu: After this new success, the question arises: the one you are interpreting, to what extent is music dedicated to a select audience?
Balázs Zságer: The definition of selective audience for me means little.
In my opinion there are two types of castes in light music; not mainstream and underground[b5], not alternative and pop, but commercial and sincere.
Also the so-called underground alternative music can be boring, meaningless and can be composed equally only for sale, which makes it commercial.
But also a good pop song can come from a sincere inspiration.
Also the attitude of listeners works in this spirit, regardless of national languages and borders.
hvg.hu: Do you see any difference between the reception of your music by the Hungarian and foreign audience?
B. Zs: Abroad, especially west of us, light music has larger traditions.
Not only the generations of fifteen and twenty years frequent the concerts, but also the oldest.
They pay much more attention to the changes that occur around them in light music, because they consider it part of contemporary culture.
hvg.hu: What role does the public have in your work?
Do you care about who they are, where they are from and how many people are listening to your music?
B.Zs: Naturally I feel good to see that more and more people are attending our concerts.
But we’ve never composed music for the market.
We don’t compose music for some purpose, but for some reason.
The role of the audience is rather felt in concerts where there is a reciprocal influence, but this is only in the inconceivable changes of the moment.
And yet I realized that if you want to meet the expectations of the public, you lose their interest.
hvg.hu: To what extent do you intend to follow Yonderboi’s example?
He works alone and made his career rather west of us.
B.Zs: We don’t follow their path, even though they sometimes try to compare our music to it.
We rather work as a team, we rely on each other’s musical presence and let it unfold.
At first it was unavoidable for them to compare our works with Yonderboi’s music, since many of us started our career in their group and from there we undertook another path.
hvg.hu: On mr2 Petõfi Wings of Love's list of hits is in first place.
Many people first heard Zagar's name in connection with this song.
Did you consciously open with this style towards a wider layer?
Zs.B.: We didn’t intend to compose big hits and sell with these hits our album.
This song is more than that.
We added it at the end of the album, trying to relax after the sound orgy of the album and the heaviest songs.
hvg.hu: How did you select the six singers?
Why precisely to them - what was the main reason?
B.Zs: The idea was to create a gospel-style choir.
Then came the idea to create this chorus of good-voiced soloists from our own national musical stage.
Thus was created that choir of six women - that i.e. Sena, Kutzora Edina, Judie Jay, Bori Péterfy, Enikõ Hodosi [Neo] and Juci Németh - which was later christened Divas of Underground.
hvg.hu: Did you compose exactly like that or did the girls change a few things?
Zs.B.: This song existed a long time ago in instrumental version and when we already had all the material of the album, we thought something is still lacking.
The chord attracted singing.
Even that night I recorded the song that the girls later learned.
Everything came practically to the first attempt and in an incredibly spontaneous way.
I remind myself, I was very excited then, but naturally I also needed the Divas.
With my voice I wouldn't have functioned so strongly.
hvg.hu: Both at the concert and on the record it looks like the girls are in the background.
There are no soloists (except Judy Jay's brief only), they have no role of their own, they sing all together and not more strongly than the music, so the music doesn't just accompany their songs.
Also on stage they are located in the background.
Intentionally?
B.Zs: They are basically simply due to technical problems.
Instead we didn’t consciously want to distribute solo papers.
The song also verses about it, that we forget for a while our ego, that where it has come from and where it goes, let those wings, the wings of love raise us.
I would have wanted to make others also feel that euphoric mood that we felt when this song was born.
hvg.hu: Which one did you dedicate more work to?
Zs.B.: In the musical composition actually none, rather when it came to mixing there were more difficult pieces.
For example the Dorian Gray's Dilemma in which I'm playing on a concert piano or the Rock'Roll Goes To The Girls, where for a long time I didn't want to work the groove and then, little by little everything went to its place as in a puzzle.
hvg.hu: What's your favorite song on the new record?
Zs.B.: This changes constantly with the concerts and because I have already "loosed" the album.
Now the Prophet Is A Fool, the Escape From The Earth and the Never The Same.
Treacherous stockbroker risks billions for inferiority complex
An embarrassing disloyal.
That’s how he points to his former employee, Jerome Kerviel, Société Générale’s French banker giant, also the owner of the Czech Trade Bank.
For him he lost about five billion euros.
However, it seems rather that Kerviel was a great player who wanted to compare himself to his colleagues and, without a doubt, with good capabilities.
He long ago intuited, unliking all the big Czech banks, the crisis in the U.S. mortgage market.
"It has a fragile character" was heard from his superiors, the sames who sent him to the police.
But what emerges from Kerviel’s responses according to the French media, such as the newspaper Le Monde, is that it was a man who at the end of last year had a profit of more than 1,600 million euros thanks to his businesses.
Crises not only in America
“All I wanted to do was make money for my bank,” he says in his answers.
Precisely, in summer, he managed to win during the American crisis, 500 million euros.
This opportunity already saw it coming at the beginning of the year.
In February some news began to be heard about so-called sub-prime mortgages offered to low-income clients or those who in the past had problems with payments and that those customers would start to have problems.
However, this crisis should not influence the entire economy.
Kerviel didn’t believe it and bet correctly.
And then, at the end of the year its profits exceeded 1,600 million euros.
"When I've already won my first 500 million I didn't know how to report it," Kerviel confesses and adds, who has left nothing for himself, at all.
Throughout the interrogation he stated that he had falsified the records in such a way that their discovery was not reached.
He even deceived the bosses, even though the Eurex Stock Exchange began to become interested in their businesses.
Risk became a benefit
Did he fear he'll discover himself?
Rather, no.
"I thought I'd earned 1.6 billion for the bank and from that simple fact, I'd make them happy."
Where did you get so much willpower to risk that way?
In my position it was to work gradually.
He went to work at Société Générale in 2000, exactly after finishing studying in Lyon.
His annual salary was handled between 51,000 dollars.
Two years later he was already an assistant stockbroker and in 2005 he became a stockbroker with an annual salary of 90,000 dollars.
I still knew that I would never win as much as everyone else.
"In my first interview in 2005 I already observed that they looked at me cautiously.
Due to my training and also to my professional and personal progress," Kerviel described the researchers.
But shortly after my entry into the company came the first great success.
Thanks to Allianz’s actions he won, during the bombings in London, playing down a 500 million euro title.
And this was a start-up mechanism, and he wanted more.
If you win, we'll leave you
"This is like a snowball," police said.
But it is said that the bosses knew about all of this or rather suspected it.
“As I made money, they closed their eyes.”
It's only that, later, came the blow earlier this year.
In a day he lost a billion euros.
After the weekend in mid-January he wanted to erase all footprints.
When he got to work on Monday, he no longer worked at the bank.
And two days later, the bank announced that it had lost 5,000 million euros because of it.
And how'd they locate him?
He became a suspect from his vacation.
"I chose only four days for the past year.
The runner who doesn't have a vacation is a runner who doesn't want anyone to take a look at his file," Kerviel concluded.
The Czech Republic has the possibility to get 365 billion
The ministers of the government of the Czech Republic signed yesterday with representatives of the European Commission a total of nine operational programs from which the Czech Republic can obtain 14 billion euros (approximately 365 billion kroners).
It is almost half of the total sum that the Czech Republic can obtain from Brussels for the years 2007 to 2013.
From seven operational programmes approximately 125 billion kroners will come out for the regions.
Czech companies will be able to obtain around 100 billion kroners from the Business and Innovation Program.
Most of the money will go into transportation, up to 150 billion.
The Transport Programme is the largest of the operational programmes and accounts for up to 22 percent of the resources that the Czech Republic can get from the fund.
This money increases the budget of the state fund for transport infrastructure that next year will have the amount of 90,800 million kroners.
The Business and Innovation program must serve entrepreneurs and companies to obtain resources in business innovation.
Businesses should obtain funding for the acquisition of new technologies, for industrial research and for the implementation of more effective organisational methods.
With regard to the current use of EU funds, the Czech Republic is among the newly-entry countries that use them least.
Twenty-year-old sentence for the former president of Nicaragua decreed the court
The Court of Appeal of Nicaragua on Thursday decreed the 20-year sentence for the former president of the country, Arnaldo Alemán, who was convicted in 2003 for the embezzlement of 100 billion dollars (almost 1.8 billion kroners).
In spite of this, some time later, he was released from prison to go to house arrest in his hacienda not far from the Nicaraguan metropolis.
It’s nothing clear right now, according to the AP agency that, the then head of the Central American state between 1197 and 2002, is back behind bars.
According to the president of the Court of Appeals, Ileana Pérez, it will depend rather on the prison agents if they let Alemán end his punishment at home or if they make him return to prison.
Four years ago, the court demonstrated how Alemán was constantly transferring government money to the account of a company in Panama.
This society was fictitious and the account belonged, in reality, to his closest relatives and supporters.
Portion of this money ended up into the fund that Alemán created to finance his campaign in the 2001 elections.
That's how they approved the budget
That's how it is.
The state budget was approved.
Why Is This Budget Special?
It is the first drawn up by this government and accepted by the majority of the coalition without the support of the opposition.
This year's budget has already been approved with the support of ČSSD, because it was prepared by Minister Sobotka and ČSSD could not afford not to accept it.
Apart from different debates before the vote on the vote of confidence to the government, this time, nothing dramatic happened.
The parliamentary assembly, in this traditional sight although the most influential, quietly approved the new law.
It's a big paradox.
Each government starts and ends with each chapter and budget item, whether they like it or not.
The budget is an important part of politics but it hides the rivalry of power between the government and the opposition.
It is important for the media and therefore they devote special attention to it.
Political discussions are much more interesting than simple numbers.
The State budgets of the last governments of the Social Democrats suffered from three flaws that for this year of 2008 it is not possible to solve so easily:
The first of these is the high participation of the mandatory laws, called as the expenses of the leaders who are not only pensions but also the social benefits that already last year were approved before the elections by the "silent" coalition of ČSSD and KSČM.
The second is the deficit in the economy as a result of the first defect.
The third limit is the deficit of public financing, such as the municipal and community budget deficit.
Despite this, the greatest risk is not in the deficit of the State Budget.
This one is public and relatively under control.
The time bomb, however, lies in the deficit of the municipal and community budget.
Many mayors in order to obtain other sources of investment, apart from money from taxes, fees and loans from banks, often issued, meaningless, obligations with which they disproportionately indebted their municipalities.
In recent years they managed to pay these debts through the mass sale of energy actions and other development networks they received from the state and privatization.
They don't currently have this resource.
If we stick only to official and verified facts, we find that:
Our economy, already a few years ago, goes through phases of growth in the same way as the rest of the world, of what ČSSD boasts.
This was the ideal occasion for his government to bring order to the state’s finances.
However, instead the state continued to indebted.
The rest of the countries, with the exception of some such as Hungary, Albania, Pakistan or Egypt, economized much more reasonably than our republic.
It is a great embarrassment that falls, above all, in the previous government.
We belong to the nations that within global measures we are less threatened by poverty.
That is why the massive social programs that, unfortunately, in recent years uselessly swelled with gigantic measures are not necessary.
And although they managed to eliminate part of the incomprehensible populist expenditures approved this year before the elections, if the retirement age and pension reform soon do not change then it will be the end of any policy in this country and, whoever governs will only be a simple bureaucracy.
Exaggerating a bit we can say that the politicians who govern will be transformed into officials, mechanical deliverers of most of the tax money for retirement and social benefits.
That’s why this year’s budget can’t be revolutionary, but it can stop the pressure of normal spending on leaders’ spending.
The planned deficit of more than 70 billion by 2008 would have been absolutely unnecessary, if the past government hadn’t wasted in the past ten years what they could.
We would not want the governing politicians to become only officials so we must be patient and grant to this weak government coalition, which realizes that the state can only spend what it is capable of obtaining from taxes and fees, the peace of mind for the preparation of other law reforms.
This alone will make it possible to gradually achieve a balanced State budget.
Jiří Krejčí
The banks want to solve the crisis
The U.S. Federal Reserve Bank, the European Central Bank and the British, Swiss and Canadian Central Banks decided to fight together against the finance market crisis.
More than one hundred billion dollars will be received in the Monetary Marking through tenders.
In these tenders the banks auction the interest rates by which they are able to lend money.
For example, the American Fed will send to tender forty billion dollars, and then another twenty-four billion will be facilitated by the central banks of Europe and Swiss.
After the September 11 attacks, it is the first time that central banks from different states have agreed on this coordinated process to protect and lessen the consequences of the finance crisis.
“This step must solve the biggest economic problem, i.e
“This coordinated action by central banks likely lowered the recession in the U.S. from 65 percent to fifty percent,” Baumohl said.
Banks have already spent sixty billion dollars on unpaid loans, especially in the United States.
Economists await billions in losses.
“Central banks must really be afraid of what’s still awaiting them when they decided to take this step,” said ABN Amro’s chief economist Kieran Davies.
"It seems that the situation is really wrong," he added.
Central banks fear that they have the same problems of access to loans and therefore will have to lend their customers more expensive.
This would reduce consumption and send the U.S. economy into recession with different impacts on the growth of the world economy.
The central banks thus decided, after they failed to reduce the so-called LIBOR fee, a London interbank fee that is used for borrowing money in the interbanking market.
This means that the banks constantly feared lending themselves money even as the U.S. Central Banks, Canada, and Britain cut their interest rates several times over the fall.
“It will have the same effect as another drop in interest rates,” Greg Salvaggio of Tempus Consulting told Reuters.
Some economists are not surprised that the step taken by central banks contributes to igniting the crisis because it does not solve the fundamental problem that is the fall of the housing market in the United States.
Klaus: Ecologist debates are incredible
Global climate change mainly affects developing countries.
President Václav Klaus again expressed himself regarding the problem of global warming.
Criticism now emerged with the closing of the U.N. international conference on climate change in Bali.
In Vienna, where he presented his book Azul, not a green planet, he remarked that the debates of environmentalists are incredible.
According to Klaus it is unacceptable not only the structure of the conference that creates a strange mixture of government representatives and non-governmental organizations but the fundamental difference between the rhetoric being used and reality.
"Breaches are barely structured there, they're fireworks of words, substitutes for the solution to current problems," Klaus said.
The Czech president during the presentation of his book stressed that this issue is very important to him and that is why he is interested.
He also expressed his joy in discovering his book translated into German because as he said "many times I only encounter the caricature of my ideas".
Now those interested can find out about their varied opinions.
Klaus recalled that he is not a climatologist but has, in his opinion, enough assumptions to write a book like this.
He is an academic, with the ability to follow and judge a specialized dissertation, has experiences with statistics and is also an economist.
At the main moment of the closure he expressed his thinking that the climate is constantly changing and that its changes are normal, that there is no agreement on global warming between scientists, that the consequences of the current changes are not so great and serious, nor do they represent possible disasters and that attempts to influence the development of the climate are useless, inefficient and expensively unacceptable.
In addition, as an experienced man with totalitarism, he considers it unacceptable to impose unproven opinions on others, which he feels as a dangerous way of limiting the freedom of others.
He repeatedly explained that he is not against "reasonable environmental defenders but against environmental activists who do not take into account the relationship between costs and benefits."
Klaus spoke in Vienna two months ago at the Hayes Institute.
600,000 people did not manage to change their driver’s license
Six hundred thousand drivers missed the date and therefore did not change their old driver’s license whose validity ends at the end of the year.
Today is the last day when people can request the change so that officials will give them time until the end of the year to issue the new card.
However, the Ministry does not fear that hundreds of thousands of drivers without the valid card are on the roads after New Year.
According to traffic, the card has not been changed mainly by those who no longer even want to drive.
While in the villages announce a rapid decline in the change of licenses, the offices of the metropolis are full of applications and interest in the new card has increased.
The City Council calculates about 2,000 daily customers.
In queues a half-hour is expected.
In Prague the new card has not yet been removed around 140,000 drivers.
The broadcast of a new card lasts twenty days.
However, it is possible to request the issuance of the card within a shorter period of five days.
But in that case the driver must pay five hundred kroners.
Drivers who are required to change their license and do not reach until the end of the year, but will hit the roads without the valid license will risk a fine from January.
The offender will pay a maximum of two thousand kroners.
The policeman can fix the infringement with an admonition.
In case of an administrative violation, the fine will amount to 2,500 kroners.
According to the above information could receive a fine, a person who does not go anywhere.
They could presumably pay up to 30,000 kroners.
The Ministry appealed to the offices to moderately enter fines of a thousand kroners, at most.
According to the member of the Ministry of Transport, Karel Hanzelka, the fines of a thousand kroners do not threaten anyone.
According to him, the driver’s license is a document in which people can decide whether or not they want it.
It is not the identity card that each person must have valid.
People who don’t want to drive should deliver the driver’s license.
It is enough to bring it or send it by registered mail to the municipal offices.
At the end of the year the cards issued during 1964 and 1993 cease to be valid.
However, drivers should gradually change the other types of driver’s license.
Individuals with the document from 1994 to 2000 have up to three years to change it.
The validity of the card that was issued between 2001 and 2004 ends in December 2013.
According to Hanzelka it is about 2.6 million more documents.
The court reduced the sentence to Berdych's accomplice detectives
Former police officers Josef Opava and Petr Koňařík accused of complicity with offender David Berdych will spend thirteen to ten years in jail.
The High Court in Prague decided as a definitive maturity the reduction of the sentences, the first to one year, and the second to two years.
Detectives in the Praguense anti-organized crime department were initially going to fall between the ages of 14 and 12.
Against today's decision can no longer be appealed, only through revocation by the High Court.
Berdych is also in this accused case, but he is expected first and foremost from the verdict of the Court of First Instance.
Despite this in other proceedings he has already been sentenced to a total of 16 years.
He can't receive more.
In January, the District Court recognized the involvement in the heist of 19 people and the higher court today revoked 16 of them.
Most of the defendants’ accusations were rejected by the investigation for being fabricated cases.
According to the Central Bohemian senate, members of the police in agreement with Berdych passed information from police sources to the criminals, covered up the robberies, and helped criminal group members avoid penalties.
These criminals handed over 30 percent of their robbery to Opava and Koňařík.
The indictment refers to criminal acts performed by the group between 1999 and 2001.
When it comes to robbery, their victims suffered serious impacts on their health but are also accused of the abuse of power as public agents and without weapons permits.
In the home search, the police founded guns, steel-cored ammunition, a laser shooter and a machine gun.
The group of criminals, according to the indictment, stole tens of millions of kroners.
Excluding nearly twenty men in this process, the court has already found Berdych and other defendants guilty.
Other men related to Berdych's case are still declaring of other processes, and in some causes they have not yet appeared.
Tomáš Půt and Maroš Šulej, who for now have avoided the trial, are in prison in Ireland where they await the final decision on their surrender to the authorities of the Czech Republic.
An account to change children: 12 million
For exchanging some children in the Maternity House the lawyer of the affected families, Igor Veleba, wants from the Třebič hospital 12 million compensatory kroner plus the expenses of the trial.
For each of the mothers, three million, for the fathers, two million, and for the children, one million.
The hospital offers at most 200,000 for each parent.
The legal representative of the hospital, Ondřej Dostál does not in principle in accordance with Veleba’s proposal.
"Such a demand we didn't approve, it's too high," Dostál said after today's meeting.
"In order for us to get an idea of this counterproposal, we need the specialist's report that the counterparty inquired to investigate.
We'll find out if it has rescisory value.
We remain in the opinion that there will be hundreds of thousands for all," Dostál said.
The amount should move between 100,000 and 200,000 kroner for each parent.
At the beginning of the cause, Jabloň’s family wanted, for every month that they did not raise their biological daughter, a million kroners.
Velaba served as the basis to negotiate compensation for the specialist's report, only that it was drawn up at Motol's faculty hospital in Prague.
The parents of the girls according to specialists in psychology and psychiatry suffered from psychic impact and stress of different levels and depth.
The stress situation was best endured by the men although they fought with recriminations over the change of the girls.
The women carry it worse with the trauma they are currently experiencing and with respect to what is happening today, Veleba completed.
Veronica and Nicola were traded by nurses at Třebič Maternity House last year on December nine.
Last week, the girls returned to their biological parents, Nicola to the Čermákový to Přibyslavic, and Veronica to Libor Brož and Jaroslava Trojanova in Jabloň.
Vysočina Governor Miloš Vystrčil delivered 100,000 kroners to each family at the end of October as compensatory expenses for the mistake made at the Třebič hospital that the region administers.
All hospitals in the Czech Republic are insured by law as liability for damages.
In case of errors they must extract from the reserve fund and extraordinarily they can ask the administrator for help.
The court until today recognized a proportionately low compensation, the sums that were calculated according to the tables that count in hundreds of thousands and extraordinarily of a million kronors.
Polívka lost the kingdom of Wallachia
Bolek Polívka lost the lawsuit over the Kingdom of Wallachian brand.
According to the judge of the provincial court of Ostrava was the first to use the brand Kingdom of Wallachia but the project was created for many years by Tomáš Harabiš with whom the actor collaborated.
Polívka didn't show up for speaking today.
According to your lawyer the case is probably not over and your client will appeal.
"The lawsuit is that Mr. Harabiš and his team are parasites to the popularity of Bolek Polívka," Polívka's lawyer said.
For him, before the words Kingdom of Wallachia, everyone comes the image of the actor and comedian.
The same idea also has Harabiš.
"We've been after us about ten years of work.
Seeking money and invening activities," he said.
For him, the cause of the lawsuit is in the money.
"After years I've realized that the project is successful and that that's why I could also receive something.
They want to live as parasites of our work," he added.
Lucrative business
According to the court, the Kingdom of Wallachia brand was first used by Polívka on his television show.
In 1993 he was crowned by actor Radoslav Brzobohatý.
So it wasn’t about orienting him towards the creation of a fictitious realm.
A few years later it occurred to Harabiš to publish the passport of the Kingdom of Wallachia.
From that comic origin resulted a business and a lucrative business activity from which Harabiš later created the society Kingdom of Wallachia.
In 1997, Polívka agreed to the use of his name and signature on passports and even offered its holders discounts to visitors to his farm and attending his shows.
Who will sit on the throne?
The judge today also determined that Harabiš only used a simple idea that Polívka made public on stage for his own business benefit.
"It is clear that Bolek Polívka helped the popularity of the Kingdom of Wallachia," the judge said.
He added, however, that in the spirit of the project is Harabiš and his team which devoted themselves to it completely.
Collaboration, among the now decomposed parts, continued until 2000 when Harabiš organized the official coronation in Vsetin for Poland.
From that moment there began to be conflicts between Polívka and Harabiš whose culmination came with the overthrow of "King Boleslav I, chosen forever".
The main role in the kingdom, through Harabiš, resulted in singer Jarmila Šuláková, as queen mother.
In 2002, Polívka filed an indictment against Harabiš and its society which until today has been rejected by the court.
Something in clear it could bring in the litigation, the tournament for the throne with its princesses, who is already preparing Harabiš.
The new king should come out of him.
He didn’t want to unveil even more data or dates.
“We’re in no hurry.
It would have to be something like the king’s path to Moravia.
The king would have to be chosen on a specific date.
Even Mr Polívka can introduce himself," Harabiš added.
Test Peugeot 207 SW 1.6 VTi: Prejudices overcome
To tell the truth I have never liked Peugeotu 206 too much.
Its walking characteristics were never anything special, the quality of the gearbox, manoeuvres and also the product could be characterized as below average.
But now there is its successor, the Peugeot 207, in the market, and it is much better.
This Combi called SW is a little more advanced and to me, I only have to think better.
When I tried the classic Peugeot 207 five doors, I complained, for example, about the header space in the back seat.
But this would be the only complaint because the Combi’s body means in this sense, that I will not suffer before two meters in length.
Flying around the world
I step inside quickly so I don't repeat it too much.
It is an elegant design where the only defect is the poor central tunnel.
Here I would further appreciate the design invention although the car already seems quite elegant.
The seats are comfortable, there are the times when we complained of short seats and backrests.
Also unliking the model 206, the lateral steering has improved considerably.
And the space, and here you can feel how the body measurements have grown.
In the Combi the aforementioned scarcity of space in the header disappears.
Suitcases to the trunk
But the main thing in this vehicle is its trunk.
This one should be valued as very accessible (thanks to the folding tailgate) and a well-distributed storage.
The dead spaces are equipped with rubber straps that are an ideal solution.
They don’t bother, and they can extend to the point of holding heavy objects.
But let's stay at the warehouse.
According to the tables, on a basic basis it has a capacity of 428 liters which compared to the competition is rather an average value.
But not compared to the best-selling vehicle in the Czech Republic, the Škoda Fabia Combi.
If we compare the 207 SW with the new generation of Mladá Boleslav model, we find that the Peugeot lags behind with its perceptible 52 liters.
From vacation abroad or when placing the stroller of the child its value is critical.
But if I had to comment something positive then I have to cite the floor that is quite flat after folding the backrests of the second line.
120 horses in four marches
Our stubborn car was equipped with a four-valve injection ignition over a capacity of 1.6 l. and a force of 88 kW.
And to tell the truth, that’s how it should look like a 1600 that disparaged the relative five doors.
It’s silent, it consumes little and above all, it has momentum.
If I compare it to the škoda era of then that it seemed as if the exhaust pipe was plugged by a rag, I can say that with it I can be impressed.
Prices respond
The price of the car is not for all pockets.
We must, however, keep in mind that we have tested an elegantly equipped vehicle with a very good engine.
The basic price of the car with injection ignition of 1400 by 329.900 kroners, you can still.
Our aggregates put it from 410,900 crowns, which is already too much.
The Premium type tested already reaches another 80,000 kroners.
Only that we would still have airbag in the headers, automatic air conditioning, automatic windshield wipers, automated rear windows...
That is, the car with everything, costs 531,900 kroners.
It’s a lot, but it counts on team add-ons in the Fabia and it’ll reach a pretty similar number.
Now it remains only to decide which of the two brands.
Slovak students are not integrated into English schools
In English schools children from Eastern European countries attend and for this reason, locals fear more changes in schools.
Integrating Eastern Europeans for now brings only a number of problems.
Even British schools register those cases where conflicts between migrants and native-born children escalate into violence.
The problem of the integration of the children of Eastern Europe into British schools is very well illustrated in the northern city of Kent where conflicts between natives and Slovak emigrants begin to grow.
Discussions, extortion and anger among students have already reached even the parents themselves.
The situation has gone so far that Chatmam police arrested a Slovak woman who was hitting a ten-year-old student with a green rod.
In his defense he said that the girl was insulting her son with slurs of racist tone.
The police also had to act after an attack by two minor girls against a Slovak emigrant.
The girls entertained him with racist slurs and threw stones at him.
"When we were going home, a boy approached us at the bus stop and started spitting at us.
When I told him to leave him he made us in addition to throwing apples and pears, and then he lowered his pants and showed us his ass "described another nasty incident for The Times, the Slovak student's mother.
Complaints are from both sides.
One of the natives even designated the conflict with emigrants in Eastern Europe as fighting for survival.
The cases already mentioned above, show us how the environment in English schools begins to be quite tense.
There are 70,000 Slovaks who came here on work in Britain.
Approximately 30,000 Slovak students attend English schools.
Cuba, the most beautiful island in the Caribbean
For visitors it really is the island of freedom.
Anything you expect from your vacation can be fulfilled, as long as you choose correctly.
Sandy and golden beaches, large waves or a quiet sea like a pond.
the palm trees and the whole included with waiters offering pizzas on the beach, icy or varied cocktails.
Kitesurfing, golf and roulette.
On the island of the Caribbean Sea you can find all of this and much more.
On an island it finds even much more and that island is Cuba, the largest and most beautiful of all the islands of the Great Antilles.
In the time of the Spaniards, Cuba became the bastion of conquest of America.
Columbus called her, the most beautiful place human eye has ever seen.
Havana became a warehouse and port of cargo of the treasures that the Spaniards extracted from America and took to Europe.
And then came the American era.
Hotel Nacional grew in the late 20's.
It was built by one of the bosses of the American mafia, Lucky Luciano, since everything there was of criminality in the United States (and therefore, prohibited) was welcomed and supported in Cuba as drugs, gambling and prostitution.
Among his guests were, among others
Winston Churchill, Ava Gardner, Frank Sinatra.
In Havana tall buildings emerged, along wide avenues ran the cars that were a symbol of worship in the 50's of the last century.
Ernest Hemingway bought a hacienda in San Francisco de Paula, near Havana, and in Cojimar had his yacht.
On the walls of Bodeguita del Medio left their signatures the stars of the world of entertainment and politicians from all over the Americas.
And today?
On the walls of Bodeguita abanense you can also leave your autograph.
In the bar of the expensive Hotel Nacional mix the cocktails according to your wishes.
And those cars already of worship of the 50's, until today they are still operating in Havana, because those Lada and Fiat who arrived have long since rusted between these humid and salty winds.
Although Havana, especially the old neighborhood is deteriorating noticeably, there are not so many wonderful colonial monuments there in the surroundings.
Other places are metamorphosed into beauty, for example, Trinidad.
Because tourism brings so much necessary money, its development is guaranteed.
In the last fifteen years new hotels grew not only in Havana but also in Varadero, on the coast of the province of Holguín and on islets such as Cayo Coco, Cayo Guillermo and others.
Cuba still offers a curiosity that is in the unique world and that is highly valued by railway lovers.
Sugar cane is transported from immense plantations to sugar factories by narrowways in steam or electrical machines.
His garages for dozens of years were not discovered and now they are there, machines that work and whose sister models in other parts of the world are only found in museums.
Where to go?
The best-known place for most visitors doesn't change.
And therefore, it is not necessary to talk more about Havana or Varadero.
Perhaps, just remember that in the aforementioned Hemingway estate there is a museum that for those who are lovers of the writer, should not stop visiting it.
The Viñales valley is the most picturesque corner of Cuba west of the island.
Lush vegetation growing in limestone land.
Mogotes, limestone pylons and rocks of high rugged in the falls of the valley, and in its grottoes fertile lands are acclimatized thanks to which roquedales that hide dense vegetation are formed.
The valley is probably where the highest-quality tobacco is grown in Cuba.
Visiting one of the cigar factories you can find your final product.
Somebody may find it interesting that the Chilean part of the series, Major Zeman, was filmed there.
Trinity
Old abolengo city that was founded not long after the Spaniards colonized the island.
Slavery and sugar brought her fame and wealth.
Wealth became beauty with constructions in the small town.
Spanish colonial architecture, especially influenced by French settlers who arrived later, in four centuries has hardly changed.
Trinidad, between the sea and the Escambray mountains, is such a secluded place that even in the 50's of the last century there was no road that linked it with the rest of the country.
Such isolation helped her stay out of the rest.
Nothing new was built and therefore, neither, nothing was destroyed, because each person was happy to have where to live.
If you have more time to be in Trinidad than a single afternoon, it is worth knowing interesting places in the nearby surroundings such as Playa de Ancón or the valley of the sugar factories.
The night belongs to the House of Music, which animates with its music the silence of the mornings.
Baracoa
A small town in the far west of Cuba, some consider it to be the most beautiful on the island.
Surely that opinion has already been confirmed by one’s path.
The two roads that reach there from Guantanamo must go through high and broken mountains, as well as a nature that barely knows the action of man.
This eastern place of Cuba has been inscribed as a World Heritage Site by UNESCO thanks to its untouched nature.
There they make the best chocolate, in their church they have the cross of Columbus (in reality it is a cross that arrived 100 years after the landing) and from the hill, where the castle was located and that now there is a hotel with the same name, you can see the mountains and among them the best known, the Anvil.
Café, rum, cigars, the Sierra Maestra, the Bay of Pigs and the island of Pinos, the Cabaret Tropicana, the patron saint of Cuba, the Virgin of Charity of the Copper, the Santería, African religion practiced by the descendants of those slaves, from all this many pages could be filled.
However, as it is said, better to see it once.
Allies are passive in Afghanistan
Few soldiers and insufficient equipment needed is what is influencing the mission’s march in Afghanistan.
NATO, according to U.S. Defense Minister Robert Gates, should devise a concrete plan for the coming years.
The mission in Afghanistan is not turning out as it was thought, Edinburgh (Scotland) the representatives of the countries that have troops in the southern part of the country.
At the same time that the conflicts with the Taliban movement are growing today, the eight participating states discuss the plans and coordination of allies.
While the U.S
“Development in Afghanistan is palpable but the armed forces can only be one of the solutions.
The next one is to enable the population that they alone can begin economic and security development," Defense Minister Des Browne told the BBC.
Ninety percent
The activity of Afghan rebels according to U.S. military data is greater than in the last five years.
The number of violent stocks grew compared to last year by 27 percent, and in Helmand province to 60 percent.
NATO countries have in Afghanistan about 40,000 troops of which a quarter are in the southern territory.
However, for the United States, allies have reached the same limit in terms of organizing and equipping units.
Exactly they ask for more helicopters, soldiers and experts to train Afghan units.
“We’ll have to seriously think about concrete goals for the future and how we’ll achieve them,” Gates said.
NATO Secretary General Jaap de Hoop also spoke today today.
"I'm not happy to know what we have on earth and heaven in Afghanistan.
“We’ve got ninety percent of soldiers and equipment we’d need, and that’s little,” De Hoop told Reuters at the close of the three-day meeting with the Japanese government in Tokyo.
Who's passive
Among the attending countries in recent months is the controversy of whether all allies do their best in Afghanistan.
For liability was criticised, for example, Germany.
"The Germans have in Afghanistan a relative number of replacements.
But they are in an area of minimal violence and the demands of struggle there are not as high as in ours, in the southern and eastern part of the country," Gates said.
The sensationalist newspaper Sun this week called German soldiers vague.
“Afghan rebels discover that the Germans are engaged in playing while our boys fight,” Sun wrote in material accompanied by photographs of German soldiers playing table tennis.
The German Bild responded to the attack and published a photograph where the British troop played a rugby match in the southern part of Afghanistan.
The debt of the State will reach a trillion in 2009
For every Czech the state owes 84,000 kroners.
Total debt amounted in September to 842.7 billion kroners.
This year the government planned to lend itself 159.200 million kroner.
However, at the beginning of December the ministry reduced the plan to 152,800 million kroners thanks to improving the evolution of the state’s budget economy.
The state debt of the Czech Republic grew at the end of September to 842.7 billion kroners.
In nine months this year it increased by 40.200 million kroners.
However, since June it declined 13.4 billion kroners.
Thus today, the Ministry of Economy confirmed its data on the state’s debt in early October.
For every Czech, the debt corresponds to 84,000 kroners.
For all last year the state borrowed more than 111 million kroners.
"For now it seems that thanks to next year's low deficit we could pass the trillion-crown border until 2009.
Next year the debt should move between 900,000 million and a trillion kroners, "said for server iHNed.cz, the economist of Patria Finance, David Marek.
Next Finance economist Vladimír Pikora also sees it: "We could spend the billion during 2009.
Exactly when that will depend on the next budget we don’t yet know.
If you saw that the situation on the political scene changed and the politicians were able to save, then it could be delayed to 2010.
But I don't see such a change," he added.
Doubt grows
The debt of the state creates debts in the central government and arises, above all, from the accumulation of the deficit of the state budget.
The state’s debt is paid through treasury bonds, state obligations, direct credits or for example loans from the European investment bank.
The state’s interior indebtedness this year grew from 38.5 billion to 719.400 million kroner.
Foreign debt for now has grown from 1.7 billion kroner to 123.3 billion kroners.
So-called negotiable state debt at the end of September contained 803.3 billion kroners and since June was reduced by 13.7 billion kroners.
The average maturity of state debt increased by 6.5 years.
"Total year-on-year debt from first to third quarter created 13 percent which is huge given how the economy works.
It is interesting that growth is generated mainly from obligations where there is 20 percent growth.
It is bad that the debt grows but on the other hand it shows that it is going to be negotiated until there is a pension reform," Pikora said.
Better than expected
From the strategy of payments and debt management of the state for 2007 it is extracted that the government planned this year to lend 159.2 billion kroner.
In early December, the ministry lowered the plan by 152,800 million kroners thanks to the improved evolution of the state budget.
The amount is composed, above all, of the deficit of the state’s budget that this year will be 76 million kroner instead of the expected 91.300 million kroners.
The rest consists of maximum resources planned for the Czech Consolidation Agency with some 13.300 million kroners, the reserve of 10 billion kroner for the payment of pensions, 43 billion kroners to finance the state’s obligations and 1.800 million kroner in payments from the loans of the European investment bank.
He compared Khartoum in front of a court today to have given a name to a teddy bear
The British teacher tried in Sudan for insult to Islam has been sentenced on Thursday afternoon by a court in Khartoum to 15 days in prison and expulsion, her lawyer said.
The Briton was accused of having left pupils aged 6 to 7 to name Mahomet a teddy bear when any depiction of the prophet of Islam is unlawful.
It was passible from a whiplash penalty.
The 54-year-old British school teacher based at the Unity High School in Khartum in Sudan, has been arrested on Sunday at her home and charged with attacking Islam and sedition, under article 125 of the Sudanese Penal Code, as a result of several complaints from parents of pupils before the Sudanese Ministry of education.
The history goes back in fact to the month of September, when this teacher asks her students, 6/7 years of age, to choose a name for the teddy bear of the class.
"Eight names come from the mouths of children, such as Hassan, Abdullah and Mohammed, "says the director of the Robert Boulos school.
Finally, after one vote in class, 20 children out of 23 have chosen Mohamed as their preferred name.
Mohamed is of course the name of the Muslim prophet, but above all a very common name in Sudan.
Then the children have made a book for the class with the photo of the bear with the following caption "My name is Mohamed".
The bear - he himself did not carry any label with this name, but the problem is simply that of the representation of the prophet regarded as an insult to Islam.
One of Gillian Gibbons’s Muslim colleagues, a teacher at the same school in Sudan, said he knew her well and would never have done anything that could be insulting towards a religious faith, “I’m sorry I’ve only asked the children to vote for a name,” it’s only an “innocent mistake.”
Opinion divided by numerous pupils of the school teacher describing her as " very attentive to her pupils " and " who never talks about religion in class ".
Remember that the name Mohamed is also the most given middle name in Britain, it is written in English with 14 different modes.
This name often chosen by Muslim families is a way to honor the prophet (often given to the first child of a family).
But what are the rules that concern the use of this name?
Can we for example give it to a toy?
This is of course a question of interpretation.
An agreement on the future status of the province, during the last session of negotiations in Vienna, has not reached an agreement on Wednesday.
In the end, failure.
The Serbs and Albanians of Kosovo ended Baden in Austria on Wednesday morning, a sixth and final session of discussions without being able to overcome their divergences over the future status of the separatist province.
"It is regrettable that the parties have not been able to reach an agreement on the statute," European mediator Wolfgang Ischinger said during a press conference in Vienna.
Emphasizing that peace in the region was “at stake”, his American counterpart, Frank Wisner, exhorted Belgrade and Pristina to respect their efforts to preserve peace and dialogue beyond the end of negotiations.
" We don't foresee violence for now but we enter into a very difficult period," he added, noting that "evident tensions exist."
End of mediation on December 10
Troica mediators, who regroup the European Union, the United States and Russia, will go one last on Monday in Serbia and Kosovo.
The future of the province populated to 90% of Albanians could become clearer when Ischinger, Wisner and Russian mediator Alexander Botsane-Khartchenko will return their relationship to the United Nations Security Council, by December 10.
Discussions in Baden, near Vienna, constituted the 6th and last session of negotiations since the troika has been commissioned by a new mediation by the UN last August.
Americans and Europeans consider that their mediation will end on December 10.
The Russians, who have already blocked the granting of independence in Kosovo in the Security Council, insist on a persecution of negotiations beyond this deadline.
“Russia was and is compromised in favor of a negotiated solution, a compromise solution,” Botsane-Khartchenko said.
Declaration of Unilateral Independence?
After eight years of U.N
Pristina feels prepared to proclaim it unilaterally if the Security Council does not resolve in its favour.
Belgrade insists on increased autonomy.
"Unfortunately, no deal has been found," the president of Kosovo's autonomous authority, Fatmir Sejdiu, announced at the Baden hotel where these "negotiations of the last chance" were held since Monday.
Hashim Thaci, former commander of the Kosovo rebellion and future prime minister of the province, has given part of his regrets.
But he added that Belgrade's plane of autonomy "belonged to a past that has led to homicides and deportations."
" Domino effect "
Serbian President Boris Tadic has considered that a compromise was always feasible, warning the Kosovo Albanian majority against the consequences of a unilateral proclamation of the province’s independence.
Belgrade particularly claims to fear an " domino effect " in a region still weakened by the wars of independence of the 1990's.
“For Serbia, he said, this doesn’t mean compromise is impossible.”
On Tuesday, the Serbian delegation had insisted that any decision belong exclusively to the Security Council, in which its Russian ally has a veto right.
" The Kosovo Parliament will have the last word "
"Only one solution within the Security Council is acceptable to Serbia," Serbian Prime Minister Vojislav Kostunica said.
" These negotiations have lasted two years.
They must end as they have begun: in the Security Council. "
To journalists, Fatmir Sedjiu had replied that " the Kosovo Parliament will have the final word on the status " , adding that any unilateral declaration of independence on the part of the Albanians would be made " in consultation " with the Westerners.
Bush opens agreement between Israelis and Palestinians
President George Bush announced, during the opening of the international peace conference gathered by himself Tuesday to Annapolis, Maryland, that the Israelis and Palestinians had finally agreed on a joint statement.
He pointed out that Israeli Prime Minister Ehud Olmert and Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas had agreed to immediately enter into negotiations in view of finding a final regulation of the 60-year-old litigious point between his two peoples.
In the presence of both men, Bush promised that he would do everything to help them conclude a “peace treaty” before the end of 2008.
Meanwhile, the Palestinians must dismantle " terrorist infrastructures " and Israel must put an end to its colonization activities, Bush said, recalling both sides of their obligations to the peace itinerary they accepted in 2003.
The head of the White House stressed that negotiations between Israel and the Palestinian Authority chaired by Abbas would try " to conclude a peace treaty that would resolve all outstanding issues, without exception, including central issues."
This denomination covers the three main tricky problems of the Israeli-Palestinian hotspot: the future borders of Palestine, the status of Jerusalem, and the fate of Arab refugees expelled from their homes during the 1948 conflict.
Taking the floor after the U.S. president, Abbas insisted that the upcoming negotiations be “global and deepened” and refer to all aspects of a regulation, citing “Jerusaleum, refugees, borders, colonies, water, security, among other things.”
Rising on his return in the gallery, Olmert committed himself to what the upcoming negotiations are "direct and continuous" and to make "an effort to conclude them in the course of 2008".
Bush fixed at the end of 2008 the completion of his " vision of two Palestinian and Israeli States " that co-exist.
Saudi Arabia revealed that it had made an effort on Bush’s side before deciding to participate in the conference.
Arabia, whose participation in Annapolis is a success for Washington, is at the beginning of a blueprint, endorsed by all Arab countries, which proposes to Israel peace in exchange for its withdrawal from all Arab territories occupied during the 1967 war, including East Jerusalem.
Annapolis marks "a point of confrontation in the history of the Middle East, more particularly because the roots of the conflict and its central aspects are attacked," Prince Saoud said in his periodic Arabic interview with Saudi capitals.
For the procurator, the police aren't responsible.
What exactly happened, last Sunday?
Just as each time in this type of events, official versions and rumors are opposed.
What are the circumstances of the accident?
According to the first elements of the investigation of the General Inspection of the French National Police (IGPN), a police car was circulating on Sunday, shortly after 17, Luisa-Miguel street, to Villiers-le-Bel.
" I was not in intervention but in patrol, and circulated at 40-50 km / h, without rotating headlight," explains a police source.
A Kawasaki-branced green motorcycle, " unapproved, i.e. unauthorised to ride on the public road " (read below) and driven by two young men without helmets, circulated " at all gas ".
“Held the police car on the left side, after a breach of the cede the step to the right,” the police said.
Control of breathalyzer practiced on vehicle occupants proved negative.
The condition of the car (the detached front, cracked windshield, ripped bumpers) testifies to crash violence.
Very quickly, yesterday morning, the procurator of the Republic of Pontoise, Marie-Thérère de Givry, announced having entrusted an investigation for " facts of involuntary manslaughter and denial of assistance " to the IGPN, collected with the departmental leadership of the public safety of Val-d'Oise.
In the afternoon, during a press conference, the prosecutor specifies that the IGPN’s investigation, to this stadium, ruled out the responsibility of the polices.
According to the magistrate three witnesses to the accident, understood on Sunday afternoon, they confirmed "the version of the police, namely that this mini-cyclet arrived relatively quickly on his left."
Yesterday, a type of slot, undoubtedly caused by rubbing of footweights on the ground, showed that both vehicles had been embedded the time for the police’s car to brake.
Vehicles have been confiscated and will be subjected to technical expertise.
The bodies of both victims have been autopsied yesterday.
What happened right after?
Yesterday, a rumor quickly circulated through Villiers-le-Bel, according to which the cops would have gone very quickly from the siege, thus not rendering relief to both young people.
The IGPN, being prudent, would also remove " any serious misconduct " concerning this point.
“It’s the most difficult aspect of research, which needs more research, about which you have to be very cautious,” a police source said.
Liberation found an eyewitness of these a few moments who have followed the accident.
One of his windows that precisely hits the scene.
" We come down immediately, with my cousin who is a nurse to the hospital, to try to revive them, says this witness.
There was nothing to do."
He then saw " a completely frightened policeman, limping.
Two others were trying to revive one of the young people, the room was talking on the phone."
Faced with the tension that quickly surrounded the scene, and, it seems, to the certainty that the people were present of the unexpected situation of the young people, the cops have been taken by car by colleagues who had arrived at the site.
Always according to this witness, the reliefs arrived "about twenty minutes after the march of the police".
They also practiced cardiac massage, in vain.
" I won't let it assume that the police services did not provide assistance to the youth.
These young people have been rescued.
Firefighters arrived immediately.
Everything has been done to try to save them," the prosecutor said.
Tension rises in Pakistan
Pakistani police on Monday suppressed the first demonstrations since the establishment of a state of emergency two days earlier by General Musharraf.
In the city of Lahore, in the east of the country, about 2,000 lawyers who protested against the measures taken within the framework of the state of urgency have been injured by the tear grenades used by law enforcement, according to witnesses.
The latter replicated with stones, injuring cops.
At least 350 attorneys have been questioned.
Scenes similar to Karachi and Rawalpindi, where police carried and injured lawyers.
Many would have been questioned.
Islamabad, Supreme Court lawyers required a general strike and announced demonstrations, as a result of a wave of some 500 arrests over the course of the weekend of opponents, male rights militants and lawyers.
The streets that gave access to the Supreme Court were blocked on Monday morning to prevent the grouping.
Other demonstrations would have taken place in Multan (center) and in Peshakar (northwest).
The lawyer movement on Monday picked up the support of regrouped religious parties in the powerful Muttahida Majlis-e-Amal alliance whose president “exchored the population to send flowers to the judges who spoke out against the state of emergency and the waste to which they were sworn in before Musharraf.”
" Musharraf's promise does not fulfill anymore "
The Pakistani Supreme Court refers directly to the measure of exception proclaimed on Saturday afternoon.
He had to speak in the coming days about the legality of the re-election to the presidential elections, on October 6, to the indirect suffrage of President Musharraf.
Court President Iftikhar Mohammed Chaudhry has been eliminated and replaced.
“Everything we assisted is illegal, unconstitutional and contrary to the Supreme Court’s rulings,” the judge told The News.
Pervez Musharraf's pledge to leave the head of the army and to become a civilian president " does not value further " after the establishment of a state of urgency, Tariq Azeem told Assistant Information Minister Tariq Azeem on Monday.
He was expected to abandon his military uniform by 15 November, the date of the end of his first presidential term.
The Assistant Information Minister also confirmed that January’s elections could be relocated.
On the other hand, the Pakistani government denied insistent rumours in the country that President Musharraf would have been assigned to residence by his deputy head of armies.
More than third of pregnancies remain unforeseen
This calculation takes into consideration unwanted pregnancies (24%) as well as ill-planned or unforeseen births.
Even today, more than one pregnancy out of every three (36%) is unforeseen, reveals a study carried out by the National Institute of Demographic Studies (Ined), forty years after the Neuwirth vote that liberalized contraception in France.
This calculation takes into consideration unwanted pregnancies (24%) as well as ill-planned or unforeseen births.
Different methods of contraception such as the pill or thirest still have a failure rate of 5% to 6%, Ined estimates.
The liberalization of contraception, however, allowed a better "domain of fertility", according to the institute which notes that the rate of use of the pill among women aged 20 to 44 is past from 5% in 1970 to 60% today.
At last, eight births out of ten would be well-planned today.
Even calculated just about a month for a couple in five and if possible for spring, season judged as the most pleasant to have a child.
Spectacular repair over the space station
It will have taken more than seven hours of work in space to astronaut Scott Parazynski and his crewmates of the International Space Station (ISS) to carry out the spectacular repair of a torn and indispensable solar panel for the continuation of the scientific activities of the station.
A risky exit that accumulated the records due to their duration, their departure from the habitable modules, from the speed with which it has been imagined, instruments "slooped" by astronauts to carry out the repair.
The problem appeared on Tuesday then that the astronauts had liberated the Harmony module from the Discovery shuttle, a thick cylindrical piece tasked with soon hosting European and Japanese scientific laboratories (see framed).
This module is a type of landing platform for laboratories.
But you have to be able to provide them in electricity.
The second task of the crew was to displace an electricity production module with solar panels weighing 17.5 tons, already present in the ISS, in order to put it in its final position.
After having displaced it, the crew began the reorganization of the solar panels of the module that have a wingspan of 76 meters.
And it’s where one of the panels, which unfold like accordions, has been damaged in just about a meter by a cable that bowed.
Deployment has been stopped so as not to further damage the panel.
The astronauts, who initially had to carry out a control exit from the Discovery shuttle, and then go to repair another solar panel whose rotation system was defective, were forced to dedicate themselves to the damaged panel.
And it is Scott Parazynski who has been chosen to go snail at the end of the 30-metre length of the teledirected arm of the shuttle added to that of the station to make the repair.
It is one of NASA's best "spacewalker."
Tall, sturdy, very skillful, has very developed torso and long arms.
At the age of 46, this training doctor has been in charge of "operating" the "wounded" solar panel.
Having inspected precisely the damage, he sectioned the fallible cable and installed types of "slats" in the damaged area.
He had been helped by the second "spacewalker" that had stayed close to the airlock and, inside, by other astronauts such as Pegggy Whitson, the commander of the crew.
The tool he used, an insulator-wrapped hockey mini-hange to prevent electrocution in solar panels that produced several hundred volts, has been conceived and “slapped” by astronauts aboard the station.
Upon completion of the operation, Scott Parazynski waited for the panel to be fully deployed before taking inventory of his instruments and returning to inside the station.
Yesterday afternoon, astronauts took advantage of a mid-rest before today, seven astronauts returned from the Discovery shuttle for the return to Earth scheduled on Wednesday.
EADS title sanctioned on stock market
The EADS share is currently in sharp decline to the Paris Stock Exchange, after the aeronautics and defense group has announced that it will have to spend between 1.2 and 1.4 billion euros to cope with the delays of the A400M.
EADS loses 4% to 21.96 euros currently to the Paris Stock Exchange.
The group has been forced to review its expectation of the operational result for 2007 in response to delays engendered by the slow progression of the engine development of the A400M, which conditions the aircraft’s maiden flight.
The cost to alleviate the delay in the delivery of the military transport aircraft, announced in October, amounts "between 1.2 and 1.4 billion euros of which more than 1 billion for Airbus", announced the mother house of the European builder EADS.
Due to these loads, EADS will be forced to announce new operating profit targets (EBITs) for 2007 during the presentation of its quarterly results next Thursday, he adds without any more encrypted accuracy.
The group also indicates that the estimation of new loads is consistent with the six-month delay.
It should be recalled that EADS operational result failed at 86% in 2006, essentially because of loads linked to delays of another programme, that of the very coarse carrier A380.
Initially, the group expected a first delivery of the A400M to the French army in October 2009.
Choosing the status quo
No surprise on Sunday, at the exit of the polls: the Russians are going to opt massively for President Poutine’s party, united Russia.
Confirming his aspiration to stability, even authoritarianism, after a very limited campaign.
Three days after the legislative elections, Russian President Vladimir Putin today directs a televised message to voters about public broadcasters, already registered but whose content is kept secret.
It does so as the leader of the list for united Russia, the pro-Kremlin party whose victory is revealed to be crushing.
Yesterday, the president didn’t let anything become transparent by receiving foreign ambassadors, being happy to deliver a new charge against the West accused of interference – his issue of predilection during the campaign.
"We know the price of a true democracy and we want honest, more transparent and more open elections, elections without incidents," he added.
According to the opposition, we are far from the truth.
Denounces a campaign stained by pressures.
Communist leader Guennadi Ziouganov says there is “never had elections so dirty, even in Eltsin’s time.”
After the crackdown on last weekend’s demonstrations, former jaque champion Garry Kasparov, sentenced to five days in prison for an illegal demonstration, visits are banned according to his lawyer.
"The Russians guarded the Soviet homo mentality"
Behind these unsurprising legislative elections are two questions much more open:
Who will succeed Poutine to the presidency?
The official newspaper yesterday published the date of the first round of the presidential election, on March 2, 2008; the candidates have until December 23 to make themselves known.
Elected in 2000 and elected again in 2004, Vladimir Putin cannot apply for the third consecutive term.
Then no successor emerges.
Which Role Will Poutine Play After March?
Prime Minister?
Head of the parliamentary majority and of the very powerful United Russia party that elected the government and the president?
Whatever it is, to the legislative elections as well as to the presidential elections, the outgoing power will triumph.
It's a tradition.
“The Russians guarded the mentality of homo sovieticus, they don’t feel masters of their fate,” says sociologist Lev Goudkov, director of Levada independent center.
The historian Nikolaï Kopossov, of the state university of St. Petersburg, goes back further: civil society was delayed in this Christianized country five centuries after Europe; the famous spirit of the community delayed the formation of individualism.
Following the liberal reforms of the 90’s, “Poutine re-established the model of a paternalistic state, perfectly accepted by the population since this new paternalism has not been followed by terrorism, but by a certain economic relief,” estimates Maria Lipman of the Carnegie Foundation.
Today the Russians " freely relinquish the personal responsibility " of those who had briefly given proof after the outbreak of the USSR.
" Why reflect? "
The phenomenon touches all social layers, including the world of affairs.
And the administrative elite plans to preserve the status quo: 65 governors (out of every 85 heads of Russian regions) run the local lists of united Russia.
New liberties imported from the West are often synonymous with chaos, as in the 90’s.
Opinion prefers stability.
In the name that the Russians will also not vote for extremists.
Conclusion of Tamara Tcherednitchenko, 54-year-old teacher: " what to reflect?
Aren’t those who are to power too bad, why change them?”
A heavy memory
After more than 60 years of confidentiality, the Nazi archives of Bad Arolsen, describing the fates of 17.5 million victims of the Hitlerite regime, are freely accessible.
The 47 million archival documents, stored on 27 km of shelves to Bad Arolsen (Hesse), were not so far consultable only in a "humanitarian" purpose, i.e
The eleven states responsible for its management - such as Germany, France, Israel and the United States - agreed in May 2006 to open them to seekers and historians.
Since the process of ratification of this agreement by all States is over, the opening is effective since yesterday.
Sensitive information
Historians’ access to Bad Arolsen will make it possible to search “particularly about the displacements of prisoners, the population of the camps and the health status of the forced workers,” explains Reto Meistern, the director of these archives administered by the International Red Cross Commission (ICRC).
Until recently, a number of States, such as Germany, were opposed to opening these nominative documents to the public, due to the sensitive nature of certain information.
As well as the alleged homosexuality or mental handicap of certain victims of deportation.
The records of the concentration camps or the arrest warrants established by the Gestapo had been gathered after the war in a practical purpose: to find the deported countrymen or subjected to compulsory work and, eventually, to provide them with proof of their internment, in order to open the way to their compensation.
Even today in Bad Arolsen, more than 300 permanent wage earners deal with tens of thousands of individual petitions.
However, for a part of the scientific community, access to Bad Arolsen is of limited interest.
“There’s nothing fundamentally new to be expected from these documents,” Professor Wolfgang Benz, director of the Search Centre on Anti-Semitism at Berlin’s Technische Universität, said in 2006.
The European Union and India want to reach a free trade agreement in 2008
Currently, Indo-European bilateral trade already reaches about 60 billion euros a year.
The European Union is India’s first trading partner and accounts for 18% of its foreign trade.
The European Union and India hope to sign a free trade agreement in 2008, European Trade Commissioner Peter Mandelson and his Indian counterpart, Kamal Nath said.
The European Union’s foreign ministers last April gave their approval to the European Commission to start negotiations with a view to signing free trade agreements (LEAs) with India, South Korea and the Association of Southeast Asian (Asean). Indo-Europian bilateral trade already reaches about 60 billion euros a year.
The European Union is India’s first trading partner and accounts for 18% of its foreign trade.
LUE is also its first foreign investor, but India is only the European Union’s 9° trading partner, according to figures from the European Commission.
“A free trade pact will very much dop both economies” and ‘India would improve its entry into a market of 450 million prosperous Europeans,’ Peter Mandelson said.
Europe represents the first or second market for each of the top ten products exported by India, said the European commissioner. The Asian and European giants change annually for "47 billion euros of goods " and for "ten billion euros of services", had declared this week Danièle Smadja, head of the European Commission delegation in New Delih, feeling that bilateral trade "has not yet reached its potential".
(Source AFP)
The Bank of England takes note of concerns offering 10 billion pounds in five weeks
Britain’s bank on Thursday was concerned to ease the current lap of concerns about credit conditions, and announced a ten-billion-pound bid to the 5.75% base index in five weeks, an unusual-duty bid.
“To alleviate concerns that financial market conditions will be particularly tight at the end of the year, and to give banks greater certainty in how they will organize their liquidity positions over this period, the Bank intends to offer a significant proportion of its expected reserve contribution during the maintenance period beginning on 6 December in the form of a five-week open market operation,” it said in a statement.
The bank specifies that 10 billion pounds (14 billion euros) will be placed on the market on December 6 at 12h a.m. GMT, the base index until January 10.
It’s the first time it looks like the England BoE bank markets liquidities for five weeks in an open market operation.
These are usually done in a week.
The BoE adds in its statement that it “is prepared to take other measures to keep interbank loan indices up-to-date in line with its base index.
The interbancy index per day was on Wednesday at 5,829%.
The after-three-month rate was set at 6.6%, the highest since September 18.
Since the beginning of the summer financial crisis, the sums placed on the market by the Bank of England were combined with a significant penalty index that had deterred banks from resorting to it.
According to certain rumors, corroborated by the evolution of the change of the pound in relation to the euro, many had preferred to subscribe to the sums brought to the market by the European Central Bank, to the most advantageous indices and with a more insured discretion.
UMP and NC parties deny examination of PS party’s propositions over purchasing power
The UMP and Nouveau Centre group refused Thursday to discuss articles of the socialist proposal of law on purchasing power, amounting to dismissal of the text.
Registered in a socialist "niche" (session for the initiative of a parliamentary group), the text declined a dozen measures adopted on Tuesday by the national office of the PS among which the 50% increase in the bonus for employment, the restoration of TIPP (indoor rate for oil products) floating, a cheque-transport or rental restrictions.
Since UMP and NC have voted against the examination of the articles (180 voices against 115), the session has been lifted at the end of the general discussion that led to exchanges, sometimes alive, between the majority and opposition a few hours after Nicolas Sarkozy’s televised intervention on purchasing power.
P.P.P. leader Jean Marc Ayrault announced that his group would represent the integrity of its proposals in the form of amendments to the Assembly’s rectifying finance bill next week.
A new festival comes to light
As a result of numerous rumors regarding the creation, by C3 Presents, of a new music festival in Philadelphia, the promoter/producer announces the Vineland Music Festival in New Jersey, in collaboration with Festival Republic by British producer Melvin Benn.
“For our company, it’s an honor to work with a person who inspired, no more and no less, the current movement of festivals in America,” Charlie Jones of C3 confided to Billboard.com.
C3 produces the Lollapalooza festival in Chicago and the Austin City Limits Music Festival.
Vineland in New Jersey is an amazing destination for camping.
The festival would take place Aug. 8-10 on a 500-acre private farm approximately 40 minutes from Philadelphia.
Formerly known under the name of Mean Fiddler, the director of the Republic Festival, Melvin Benn, is one of the most respected festival producers in the world.
In 1989, he took the direction of the Reading Festival in the United Kingdom, which annually attracts about 80 000 people.
In 1999, Melvin Benn added the Leeds Festival to its portfolio later, in 2006, the Republic Festival created the Henham Park Latitude Festival at the Suffolk.
Since 2002, as co-owner, Melvin Benn was also responsible for the production, licensing and organizing tasks of the Glastonbury Festival, which can now accommodate up to 177 500 people.
Qualifying Glastonbury's " most inspiring event " he's ever attended, C3's Charlie Jones says his company and Melvin Benn's are working in parallel to give the region a European-style festival-event.
“We had chosen Philadelphia as a marketplace and were persistently working with the Fairmount Parks Commission to create a festival in downtown Philadelphia.
" We were in negotiations with the city and the Commission was motivated and excited about this project.
Unfortunately, we stagnated in low-level policies because of today’s administration, Charlie Jones pursues.
“Luckily, we were able to argue with Melvin Benn and we were preparing to create a magnificent festival in an exceptional site that, lately, will take place in Philadelphia.”
C3 Presents resurrected the Lollapalooza festival in 2005 at Grant Park in Chicago, having unraveled into the landscape of the festivals in 2002 with the Austin City Limits Music Festival.
Both events recorded respective $9.8M and 11.3M$ gross revenue in 2007.
These two festivals take place in an urban environment.
“Melvin Benn’s European model is a country festival, while ours are held rather in urban greens,” says Charlie Jones.
The objective is to merge, in one way or another, both formulas to give at the same time an impression of country festival in the European and urban manner in the American way. "
Vineland is more or less halfway between Philadelphia and Atlantic City.
“The Vineland community, including the mayor, enthusiastically supports the celebration of this event,” says Charlie Jones.
The latter refuses to reveal the conditions of the agreement, but states " that they are quite interesting to allow investment in such an event and host a festival that, we hope, will have a long life."
Charlie Jones says the hotel offer of this festival is "very large", in the example of that of 80 000 people from the Bonnaroo Music Festival in Tennessee.
He says that invitations have been thrown at the groups, but that nothing could still be confirmed at the time of going under the press.
“Vineland will have the taste of rock, but the music will be varied there, hoping to attract all sorts of viewers,” says Charlie Jones.
His C3 teammates, who received the Top Independent Promoter Award from the latest Billboard Touring Awards, are Charlie Walker and Charles Attal.
Montray faces Terminator
It’s not easy to lure Hollywood movie dishes into Montreal when nothing but Terminator opposes that...
This seduction mission is part of delegation functions.
One mandate - "politically difficult" because California Governor Arnold Schwarzenegger denounces "runaway productions."
Is it difficult to compete with the "Governator"?
"You have to be cautious, it's the industry that decides where it's going.
If you find that the conditions in Montreal are favorable, you will go there.
Our role is to offer those who are going to judge the best,” he says.
The Race to Festivals
At the moment, Denis Turcotte’s priority is despite the promotion of the cinema here.
The race to the Oskares is begun.
All West Coast festivals, whether Sundance, Denver, Seattle or San Francisco festivals, will have to present the Quebec movies, give them value and make sure for the filmmakers to do interviews.
The Age of Darkness had a good image at the 30° Mill Valley Film Festival, a few weeks ago.
It will be presented to the Palm Springs International Festival in January.
Shake Hands with the Devil is in Santa Monica and will be presented at the 30th Starz Denver Film Festival in November.
Quebec also unveiled four feature films and four short films to the American Film Institute Fest this month.
Is there an end-of-year rally on the market? Experts, divided by the ‘subprime’ crisis.
Less than five weeks to lay off, investors are already rubbing their hands waiting for the traditional end-of-year rally.
However, this year the experts are not so clear that it is going to occur.
Banif believes that "from a statistical point of view, the month of December on the stock market usually has positive behavior.
However, it is not advisable to make forecasts based exclusively on statistics, even more so because in the current context, uncertainties lurk in markets, at least in the short term."
Although they are not in favor of the stock market laiming rags in the last weeks of the year, these experts point out that "the stock market is sustained by the existence of liquidity, willing to invest given the lack of alternatives with guarantees, especially the fixed income, affected by the flight effect towards quality values in both the long and the short tranches."
Therefore, they believe that the exchange will have a rather lateral behavior, not without volatility "especially since the impact of the likely decline of the Fed's rates is not known, given the high level of crude oil and the danger of stimulating inflationary tensions."
Javier Barrio, head of BPI sales in Spain, agrees that it is not a good time to venture to say that there will be a rally.
“There’s not the thing for a lot of joy,” he said.
The Ibex has lost close to 4% since the highs scored on November 8 when the index closed at 15,945.7 points.
Yet not all experts have such a negative view.
Juan Solana, an analyst at Intermoney, believes that the Ibex 35 could close the year closer than 16,000 points thanks to the restructuring of the portfolios and the traditional contributions to the pension plans that occur every year at this time.
However, the expert qualifies that things will be somewhat different this year as he believes that the rally will be ahead of the second week of December, after the bridge of the Constitution.
The analyst does not consider that volatility will affect the market trend.
For his part, Federico Olucha, an analyst at Inversis Banco, assesses that we are close to technical levels and "therefore we could see a rebound of the index that could be driven depending on news coming from the United States regarding the consequences of the crisis in the credit market."
The analyst is confident that these are positive.
Analysts agree when choosing the values that will be responsible for taking Ibex towards new maximum heights.
Solana, of Intermoney, states that "this year it's up to great values."
The expert would include in the portfolio the two big banks and some construction companies "because when the date arrives, the electricity sector will be very expensive".
Meanwhile, Federico Olucha of Inversis Banco assures that the increases will come hand in hand with banking and the industrial sector.
The construction companies will also be able to benefit from this rally, in case they give.
"ACS has been regaining positions for several months and we expect other construction companies such as Ferrovial and FCC to follow their same path," he said.
Cyclical consumption will be the protagonist in the last part of the year due to the increase in sales in the holiday sales season.
On the other hand, the expert believes that technologies will also do very well although in this case there is not much representation in the Spanish market.
Five times in seven years
In the last seven years, on only two occasions December has been a bearish month.
The authentic year-end rally was experienced in 2003, a year in which stock markets emerged from the crisis caused by the puncture of the technological bubble.
This year, in which the Ibex 35 regained 28.17%, December registered a rebound of 6.68%.
We will have to see if 2007 is the fifth consecutive year of profits (for the moment the Ibex rises 8.36% since January) and if it manages to count on its year-end rally.
Popular will open 200 offices 12 hours from Monday to Saturday
Popular has decided to renovate much of its offices.
A total of 200, those located in the most commercial areas in Spain.
These branches, which will operate under the Popular Max brand, represent a big change for the bank.
Also for the rest of the Spanish entities, since it is the first group that decides to make the leap to bet on the uninterrupted opening of their agencies until 20.30 in the afternoon, and open on Saturdays from 10 hours to 20.30 in the afternoon.
Another group that has also reiterated on several occasions that it wanted to extend the schedules of its branches, BBVA, has not yet decided to take the step.
Meanwhile, it’s about to close an agreement with unions to close 75% of their offices on Saturdays in exchange for opening an afternoon, albeit not to the public.
The results of Popular’s experience will be decisive for other entities to sign up or not for this initiative that supports the schedules of shops.
Precisely this is the goal that Popular pursues with the project.
Capture the private customers who move through these areas to make their purchases, to SMEs, self-employed and shops on the streets chosen to open.
The bank wants to have these 200 offices open throughout Spain in about 18 months, since they are not new openings but remodeling of the already existing ones.
To do this, the entity will modernize the branches it already has in commercial areas, adapting them to the profile presented by customers of the different streets.
In this way, the extension of the schedules is accompanied by a different conception of the space of the branch and a new design, more current, with brighter colors.
The head of commercial banking, Ángel Rivera, assures that this restructuring does not represent a great investment, although if a greater hiring of personnel, since it goes from having about six employees per premises to eight or nine.
The offices, which will even have spaces for SMEs to meet there, will sell non-financial products.
A positive experience for the group
Popular has already tested its initiative in three offices in Madrid.
And the experience has been positive, according to Ángel Rivero.
The branches of Bravo Murillo, O'Donnell and Gran Vía in Madrid have been chosen, and it seems correctly, according to Rivero.
Popular currently has 2,500 branches.
And another 60 that operate under the Mundocredit brand, specialized in immigrants, also with very wide schedules, which even open on Sundays and holidays.
In these premises of PopularMax they will not repeat the BBVA model, where several of its offices have a wide range of non-financial products for their sale.
“We don’t want to do the competition to our customers,” Rivero said.
At the moment, they have reached an agreement with Telefónica to sell mobile phones, with staff external to the bank.
Telecinco doubles for the first time the stock market value of its rival Antena 3
We've done it.'
With that phrase expressed his satisfaction yesterday Paolo Vasile, CEO of Telecinco, at the close of the market, when he found that the chain that directs doubled the value of his rival, Antena 3.
Only one aspect clouded his joy: 'it's what hurts me, it's not because we've grown up more but because we've come down less," he said.
Even so, he stressed that in a weak market, ‘we’ve fallen less.’
Telecinco ended the day yesterday with an advance of 2.54%.
That gain places its loss so far this year at 15.66%.
The stock market value of the company controlled by Mediaset (with 52% of the capital) and owned by Vocento (another 13%) thus reaches 4,488.88 million euros, according to Bloomberg data.
His rival Antena 3, which yesterday fell 1.52% and accumulated a decrease of 40.5% since January, costs half, 2,193.46 million.
The value of the other listed communication companies amounts to 3.571 million in the case of Sogecable; 2,518.53 million Prisa (Five-Day publisher) and 1.779 million Vocento.
According to Vasile, the comparison to Antena 3 is because 'we're talking about two similar companies.
The relative fact is how much we are able to do, in the same market, at what cost and how we make it profitable in terms of audience.”
Telecinco announced last week that it expects to become the first television network this year to exceed one billion gross advertising revenues, said Giuseppe Tringali, the CEO of Telecinco and Publiespaña, the subsidiary that manages the group’s advertising.
If this announced data becomes real, the television network would record this year an increase of 3.6% in its advertising turnover compared to 965.4 million in 2006.
Meanwhile, the net turnover of Antena 3 increased by 1.6% in the first nine months of the year (to reach 734.4 million) while net television revenue grew by 0.7% (630.4 million).
One of the factors that analysts point out for the best relative evolution on the Telecinco Stock Exchange is the high pay out that it has maintained so far: in 2006, the company chaired by Alejandro Echevarría distributed 100% of the profit among its shareholders.
Vasile assures that, although it is early to make the decision, this ratio could vary after the purchase of 33% of Endemol in association with its Mediaset matrix.
"We have an official commitment to give at least 50%, although we have always declared much more.
This year, I hope we will be able to leave our shareholders happy, to whom we have already gaven value with 33% of Endemol.
According to analysts, the market demonstrates at this time a certain fatigue.
Lehman Brothers recently lowered its Telecinco profit estimates in 2008 by 4% and in 2009, by 7%.
It is due, they explained, that it has cut expected revenue growth from 10.5% to 8.4 per cent in 2008 and 5.5 per cent to 5.1 per cent in 2009.
This same firm has lowered Antena 3’s profit forecast by 4.5% in 2008 and by 7.5% in 2009.
3 reviews
1.
Ibersecurities: recommends buying both securities based mainly on their high dividend profitability and long-term sustainable potential.
2.
Caja Madrid: sees Telecinco better (accumulating) than Antena 3 (keeping) because of the 'attractive multiples' and rise of the business.
3.
JPMorgan: recommends infraponderation in both cases by having 'similar threats' (saturated market and worse economic climate).
Congress approves mifid transposition, which went into effect 1 November
Parallel to its parliamentary process, which ended today with the vote by the Congress of the amendments incorporated into the bill in the Senate, the Government has submitted to public hearing the regulation that will develop the new law, with the objective that both come into force before the end of the year.
The representatives of the different groups agreed to highlight the effort made by deputies and senators to negotiate and agree on the best regulations in order to ensure the protection of investors and regulate in detail the activity of the entities so that the markets function efficiently.
The Mifid, which amends the Securities Market Act, involves the modernisation of financial markets, while strengthening investor protection, improving the supervisory powers of the National Securities Market Commission (CNMV) and fostering cooperation between the various supervisors of the European Union.
The new regulations will make it possible to provide financial advisory services to both specialized firms and natural or legal persons and creates a new type of financial services firms (ESIS), financial advisory companies (AFIs), which join securities companies, securities agencies and holding companies.
In addition, it expands the number of systems for the execution of transactions on financial instruments, so that regulated secondary markets are joined by multilateral trading systems and internalization order systems, which will compete with current exchange managers.
The Law also obliges investment firms to disclose in the market information on key aspects of their business profile, exposure to risk and forms of risk management and requires them to keep track of all operations they carry out, to facilitate supervision by the CNMV.
In its passage through the Congressional Economy Committee, several modifications were incorporated, among which it emphasizes that securitized debts are considered as a "complex" financial instrument given its high danger to the investor, which has been demonstrated with what happened with U.S
In addition, the transposition of the directive to legally delimit the functions that can be carried out by graduates in Economics and Business 30 years after the adoption in 1977 of the royal decree delimiting the professional functions reserved for economists was approved.
For its part, the Senate incorporated the creation of new figures in the financial sector, such as that of the mediator, who will work for others, will not require authorization the CNMV and will be able to provide its services of marketing of products and attracting clients to different investment companies at the same time.
Harmonised CPI increases five-tenths in November to 4.1%
This indicator, which later serves Eurostat to incorporate it to the calculation of the inflation index in the European Union, provides an advance of how prices evolved in Spain during the month of November.
Its publication responds to the policy of Eurostat and the European Central Bank (ECB) to offer data comparable in time and quality to those produced in the United States.
The forward indicator is calculated using the same procedure as the employee for the Harmonized Consumption Price Index, but using various statistical modeling methods to estimate the information not yet available at the time of publication.
The INE recalled that the information provided by the advanced indicator is only indicative, so it does not necessarily have to coincide with the definitive data, which will be released on December 14.
"CPI will continue at relatively high levels"
The second vice president and economy minister, Pedro Solbes, has affirmed that the 4.1% rise of the CPI in November is a "temporary figure", but at the same time has predicted that the price index will continue at "relatively high" levels in the coming months.
In any case Solbes has pointed out in the corridors of the Congress that "although the figure is not good" Spain's inflation differential with respect to the monetary union remains "more or less" the same in recent years.
He also explained that in November "there has been less surprise" than in the previous month, when the government did not have such a high rise.
"We expected a figure at around 4%," the economy minister acknowledged with respect to the data advanced today.
Viring plans to raise 42,000 million euros with Northern Rock in three years
Northern Rock deposits have fallen more than 50% to 12,000 million pounds (16,800 million euros) since it went into crisis in mid-September and had to resort to an emergency loan from the Bank of England.
At that time he amassed record deposits above 25,000 million pounds, a figure that has fallen progressively in two and a half months due to the distrust of his customers and despite the one hundred percent guarantee of that money offered by the Government and that it will maintain until the end of the crisis.
Virgin, which would rename the bank with its financial trademark Virgin Money, needs to account for about a quarter of revenues at British banks deposited over the next three years to get those remaining 18,000 million pounds to reach the target of 30,000 million.
Tycoon Richard Branson’s group, known for its eye-catching advertising campaigns in the UK, intends to spend 50 million pounds (about 70 million euros) annually on advertising and marketing to achieve its purpose.
Northern Rock this week named the Virgin consortium’s offer, in which three other companies participate, such as his favorite to bail him out of bankruptcy.
Detained the mayor of Totana for alleged plot of urban corruption
The Civil Guard has arrested the current mayor of the Murcian municipality of Totana (of the Popular Party) for his alleged relationship with the plot of urban corruption uncovered this week.
In addition, one of the secretaries of the consistory and the police chief of the municipality have also been arrested.
José Martínez Andreo replaced last May Juan Morales, current popular deputy, and until then mayor of the municipality, and who according to sources of the investigation consulted by Cadena SER, could be the 'role' of this plot.
The agents continue to register the municipal units and the Ministry of Urbanism and no further arrests are ruled out in the coming hours.
In addition, the lawyer of Juan Morales has been imputed, the main suspect in the plot of urban corruption uncovered earlier this week.
As yesterday the Cadena SER reported, the lawyer of the 'popular' deputy Juan Morales, therefore strengthened, was arrested leaving the home of Morales with important documentation related to the plot.
Moreover, the object of the investigation, according to sources of the investigation, is the alleged collection of commissions of Morales in exchange for facilitating the signing of an urban agreement with a Galician construction company to requalify 200 hectares of land.
At the moment, there are eight people arrested.
Bono agrees to spearhead the PSOE’s candidacy for Toledo and preside over the Congress if they win
Former Defense Minister José Bono has accepted the offer of the president of the Government and general secretary of the socialists, José Luis Rodríguez Zapatero, to head the list of the PSOE for Toledo for the next general elections and to be president of the Congress in the event that the socialists win the general elections.
This has been announced at a press conference by the secretary of Organization of the PSOE, José Blanco, and Bono himself, after the meeting he held this noon at the federal headquarters of this party with Zapatero.
The head of the Executive has justified the offer to the former minister because "it is important to have the best" in political life and Bono "is among the best."
In addition, he has pointed out that "yes it seems" that the Manchego politician will be the candidate of the socialist group to preside over the Congress if the socialists expire in the next elections.
Bono would replace as president of the Congress Manuel Marín, who made public on November 15 his decision not to run for the next general elections and to abandon his career in active politics to dedicate himself to fighting against climate change in the university environment.
The former minister has acknowledged that the president of the government has not stopped insisting that he return to the political forefront since leaving it two years ago.
In addition, he has pointed out that, just as citizens know who will be the economic vice president if the PSOE wins the elections, his party has wanted to announce who will chair the Congress, in an "act of transparency".
If he reaches office, Bono hopes to turn the Chamber into "the house of respect and not of insult or scream." and to make him "more and more like citizens."
"Sometimes unfortunately it seems that the only venue in Madrid where you can't speak quietly and calmly is Congress, the president of the Government was once interrupted in the Senate 26 times."
Likewise, he has had words of praise for his current president, Manuel Marín and "his good work" and has not already wanted to see himself occupying his position so as not to fall into what, he has pointed out, his adversaries could see as "arrogance".
Climatic propaganda
Since the anti-climate change movement undermines both skeptics of their predictions and those who prioritize other political and social battles, it is bound to show iron coherence.
And more a leader of the movement who is president of the Government as Zapatero and believes that this struggle is more important than that of Islamist terrorism and even intends to sign a "new contract with the planet".
This approach obliges him to explain why his government’s action, or inaction, has decisively contributed to Spain leading the EU in non-compliance with Kyoto.
Who are responsible for the non-compliance, in which sectors it has occurred and why its Government, that of the contract with the planet, has not avoided it.
In addition, it requires him to explain with the utmost clarity to the Spaniards what are the measures he will take to curb climate change.
Which companies will be affected, what citizen habits must be changed, what individual and collective energy savings we will be obliged to do, what economic consequences it will have.
I mean, who will sacrifice and who will pay to save the planet.
But there hasn't been or will be such explanations.
Precisely because it’s about sacrificing and paying.
Measures against climate change, real measures are unpopular.
Expensive, awkward and threatening to the accounts of companies and individuals.
Even the cent of gasoline suggested by the PSOE has seemed so dangerous electorally to Zapatero that he has rushed to deny it.
I mean, it's about saving the planet with nothingness, with sheer propaganda, with empty slogans of all real consequences.
With shocking phrases, commissions, committees, protocols, new positions.
With contracts with the planet, that gentleman so useful for electoral campaigns that neither speaks nor denounces nor demands, but adorns the rallies and inspires tenderness.
As long as it is limited to being a purely virtual contracting party and does not pretend that we travel by bike or refresh ourselves with the fan.
Detained the mayor and the head of the local police of Totana for an alleged plot of urban corruption
The Civil Guard has arrested the mayor of the Murcian town of Totana, the "popular" José Martínez Andreo, the head of the local police, the secretary of the City Council and a hospitality businessman for possible urban crimes, have reported today sources of the investigation.
The mayor was arrested at home and has been transferred to the Consistory, in whose dependencies he is currently together with numerous agents, who have also gone to the Department of Urban Planning and to the municipal company of management of Industrial Land and Housing.
These three arrests are in addition to the six carried out last Monday in Galicia, Murcia and Madrid, in an operation related to the requalification of more than 2 million hectares of rustic land in urbanizable for the Galician company Nuaria to build 4,000 homes, after the payment of illegal commissions during the last legislature.
In addition, two other people were not arrested but are charged in the summary, which instructs Court No. 1 of Totana.
The first six detainees have gone to court today.
As reported by the sources, the former mayor of Totana and now autonomous parliamentarian of the PP, Juan Morales, is being investigated.
In addition, the ex-wife, owner of a real estate agency registered today in Totana, has been imputed, as has the current girlfriend of the former mayor, who resides in Murcia capital.
The director and owner of the Nuaria Group, lawyer and businessman Manuel N.A., was arrested in Nigrán (Pontevedra), as well as Pablo José M.G., director of Suelo de Inmonuar, an agency integrated in the aforementioned Group, and through which the bribes would have been carried out.
The investigation is carried out by the Urban Crimes Group of the Central Operational Unit (UCO) of the Civil Guard, whose agents, in addition to the arrests, practiced eleven searches, the majority in companies related to the detainees and located in Madrid, Vigo, Murcia, Pontevedra, Las Rozas (Madrid) and Totana.
A single person was then arrested in Totana, in particular, the owner of a well-known poultry company in the region, who could have acted as an intermediary.
The Nuaria Group was in charge of developing what would be the largest residential complex in the Murcian municipality of Totana, which would involve the construction of more than 5,000 homes, a golf course and two hotels with "spa".
The company acquired in Totana 2.2 million square meters of land that were requalified and its project would mean doubling the population of the municipality, which has 25,000 inhabitants.
The Nuaria Group integrates companies such as Autesa and Inomonuar, dedicated to real estate development; Conycase, which manages the Viguese car parks of Coruña, Venezuela and the square of Fernando el Católico; Hogartel, dedicated to the direct marketing sector; It advocates, focused on the promotion, sale and installation of construction elements.
