A colleague passes information on the introduction into the Criminal Code of Internet Download Crimes:
A. Unloading a song would be a crime with a penalty of six months to a year.
On the other hand, if you steal in the store discs worth less than 400 euros, it is simply considered missing (article 623.1).
B. If you steal in the store up to 1,000 euros, the theft is already an offence, but the penalty is still lower than that imposed on discharge (article 234 of the Criminal Code).
C. If you steal a car and return it 40 hours later, the penalty is still lower than the unloading (Article 244.1).
D. It is less serious to participate in a fight than participating in compact exchange.
Participating in a tumultuous quarrel has a penalty of three months to one year (article 154 of the Criminal Code) and the exchange would have a sentence of six months to two years
(art. 270 of the Criminal Code).
E. Sexual harassment at work is considered less serious than downloading a movie on DVD, according to article 184.2 of the Penal Code.
F. The distribution of films protected by copyright and unauthorised by authors is more punished than the distribution of pornographic material to minors (article 186).
Anyway, if my colleague's right, someone's going this hand, a very long hand.
